1: # QUALITY — kumitate admission bar
2: 
3: Claim admission for this lane lives here. Tier definitions live in
4: `corpus/SOURCES.md` per the frozen fleet contract `SOURCES-CONTRACT-v1` rule 3;
5: the research method stays chousa's. A criterion is a gate: an entry that misses
6: one is rejected or held, and the reason is kept in the round's `## Gate`.
7: `SCORECARD.md` line pointers below resolve at `16a5441` (the base this file was
8: written on); `LOG.md` and lesson pointers resolve at any later revision.
9: 
10: ## Entry criteria
11: 
12: - **Q1 — header triple.** Top of every admitted entry: `source:` (S### ids,
13:   URL, exact anchor), `verified-at:` (ISO date plus the revision/version
14:   observed), `recheck:` (a re-runnable command or citation). A missing header
15:   is a reject. Grounding: the "Unadopted contract surfaces" row in
16:   `corpus/lessons/round-34.md` (pre-round: 38 of 38 knowledge notes lacked the
17:   triple; 0 `recheck:` lines).
18: - **Q2 — every external fact cites an opened `corpus/SOURCES.md` row.** Tier C
19:   is never sole support; `community` is never tier A (tiers are scoped, per
20:   `SOURCES-CONTRACT-v1` rule 3). Grounding:
21:   `corpus/lessons/round-18.md:32-40` — the first wave was rejected with 80
22:   citation-form errors and re-admitted only at 0.
23: - **Q3 — every count carries its counting command and a dated re-run** (for
24:   this admission round, 2026-10-19), or an explicit `recalled` label. Grounding: SCORECARD.md:1197-1208 ("a recalled
25:   count is a claim; re-run it or label it as recalled"); the round-34
26:   "Recalled counts" and "Stale prose" rows.
27: - **Q4 — inferences are labelled `[INFERENCE]`; unknowns are named UNKNOWN.**
28:   Grounding: `corpus/lessons/round-18.md:60` (binary-strings evidence labelled
29:   INFERENCE-from-docs rather than passed as observed behavior).
30: - **Q5 — secret/credential-bearing surfaces are shape-only**: stat facts
31:   (size, mode, mtime), never content; no credential material, password-manager
32:   secret references, tokens, or private URLs. Grounding:
33:   `corpus/lessons/round-19.md:41-44` (shape-only covers durable artifacts and
34:   transient output; "count, never print values").
35: - **Q6 — gate-clean.** The entry adds 0 cite-check errors (per-file command in
36:   How to apply) and any gated family it touches reads MATCH on the strict/row
37:   check, not just the aggregate. `CLAIMS: MATCH` alone is not
38:   section-honesty. Grounding: `corpus/lessons/round-19.md:69-73` (errata
39:   added fresh citation errors; the sweep ran after, not before) and the
40:   round-34 "Gate blind spot" row (LOG.md:1297).
41: - **Q7 — a DRIFT line that motivates the entry is quoted whole, with its
42:   date.** Never a summary of the terms. Grounding:
43:   `corpus/lessons/round-20.md:35-44` (a summary glossed two causes; the
44:   durable rule became full-line capture) and LOG.md:1048.
45: - **Q8 — version skew is named.** When a fact comes from upstream `main` or
46:   current docs, name the installed host binary/version actually observed and
47:   the revision gap. Grounding: `corpus/lessons/round-15.md:91` (the origin
48:   tree moves under the citations; re-probe, do not trust) and
49:   `corpus/lessons/round-20.md:71` (OMP re-census parked as carried debt).
50: - **Q9 — one domain.** Cross-domain evidence is reported, not absorbed
51:   (PROVINCE Refuses). Grounding:
52:   `corpus/lessons/round-5-aggregator-mirror-out-of-province-membrane-seal.md:24`
53:   (no owning province: route to the integrator/operator, do not fix locally).
