55: ## Round criteria
56: 
57: - **Q10 — the round record passes the lane's own `scripts/round-gate.mjs`
58:   before close.** A `##`-section record that the gate cannot parse is DRIFT,
59:   not a completed round. Grounding: the round-34 "Own round-gate fails own
60:   record" row (live `--round 32` → 3 errors, exit 1).
61: - **Q11 — every landed candidate has a dated LOG admission entry** naming the
62:   round identity, the work revision and the gate lines. A commit without the
63:   entry is an unadmitted candidate regardless of its content. Grounding: the
64:   round-34 "Admission-status ambiguity" row (SCORECARD.md:378,458; `16a5441`
65:   unmentioned in LOG.md/SCORECARD.md).
66: - **Q12 — every round commit carries the lane identity**
67:   `kumitate-shokunin <kumitate@shokunin.local>`, verified at close with
68:   `git log --format='%ae' | sort | uniq -c`. Grounding: the round-34
69:   "Attribution / identity defect" row (2026-10-19 histogram: 26 lane of 75).
70: - **Q13 — DRIFT at round open is re-run and dispositioned before close.**
71:   Run `scripts/proxy-check.mjs` and `scripts/kimi-census.mjs` at open; capture
72:   the full line with its date; name each term's disposition. Grounding: the
73:   round-34 "Substrate mutation" row (LOG.md:1015-1017, 1048) and Q7.
74: - **Q14 — evidence pointers never live under `/tmp`** and never use the
75:   pre-move lowercase `projects/` path; they are repo-relative or under the
76:   live repo root. Grounding: the round-34 "Dead pointers" row (15 lowercase
77:   paths in LOG.md; 6 + 2 `/tmp/kumitate-r*` pointers).
78: - **Q15 — origin-tree counts name their pinned revision.** Every count read
79:   from the upstream tree (S/R members, sections, anchors) names the immutable
80:   revision it was measured at, taken from a private read-only clone pinned to
81:   that revision, never the operator's moving checkout; a pre-registered number
82:   is re-measured at round open before work starts. Grounding: the round-35
83:   "Pre-registered baseline measured on a tree that then moved" row
84:   (`corpus/lessons/round-35.md`; 91/91 pre-registered, 86/88 measured).
85: 
86: ## How to apply
87: 
88: Run from the lane worktree; capture each full verdict line and its date.
89: 
90: 1. **Open.** `node scripts/proxy-check.mjs`; `node scripts/kimi-census.mjs`;
91:    `node scripts/round-gate.mjs --round <N> --reports-dir .ufo/reports
92:    --main-repo .`. Quote every DRIFT line whole; disposition each term before
93:    close (Q7, Q13).
94: 2. **Admit an entry.** Check Q1-Q5, then the per-file citation delta (Q6):
95: 
96:    ```sh
97:    node scripts/cite-check.mjs --json 2>/dev/null | node -e 'let s="";process.stdin.on("data",d=>s+=d).on("end",()=>{for(const f of JSON.parse(s).files){const e=f.findings.filter(x=>x.severity==="error").length;if(e)console.log(e,f.file)}})'
98:    ```
99: 
100:    The entry's file must print 0. Then the strict row:
101:    `node scripts/claims-check.mjs --row <ID> --strict` → `CLAIMS: MATCH` with
102:    `adv=0`, plus `node scripts/proxy-check.mjs` for the section count.
103: 3. **Verify counts.** Re-run the counting command today; put the command and
104:    date in the entry, or write `recalled` (Q3).
105: 4. **Verify pointers.** No new hit for the entry in
106:    `grep -rn '/tmp/kumitate-r\|vgpnk/projects/' LOG.md SCORECARD.md corpus`
107:    (Q14).
108: 5. **Close.** `node scripts/round-gate.mjs --round <N> --reports-dir .ufo/reports
109:    --main-repo .` → `ROUND_GATE: CLEAN`; add the dated LOG admission entry
110:    naming round identity, work revision and gate lines (Q10, Q11); verify the
111:    identity histogram (Q12).
112: 6. **Reject or hold.** Record the candidate, the criterion it missed and what
113:    would flip the verdict in the round's `## Gate`; a rejection is taste
114:    evidence, not an omission.
115: 
116: ## Post-review clarification (round 34)
117: 
118: Q1 still applies to every new admission. The no-header legacy count is limited
119: to the 38 direct `corpus/knowledge/*.md` identities present at frozen base
120: `16a5441`, listed immutably in `scripts/sources-check.mjs`; those paths remain
121: exempt-but-counted even when later text is appended. Appended text in one of
122: those files is not a new sourced entry and cannot support an expansion claim.
123: Any non-base knowledge path without a nonempty `source:`, `verified-at:`, and
124: `recheck:` trio fails the source gate.
125: 
126: - **Q16 — a gate that admits anchors is checked against symbol-on-line truth before landing.**
127:   A fidelity term whose pairing can be satisfied by shifting an anchor onto a neighbouring symbol
128:   is not a fidelity gate. Before a green line is cited as anchor truth, re-measure the moved
129:   anchors with an independent parser against the pinned revision (`corpus/lessons/round-36-verifier-spotcheck.md`
130:   D1/D2; round-36 lost 123 previously true anchors this way). The check must be a committed command with its recorded output — a throwaway
131:   parser or the gate's own CLEAN line is not evidence for this criterion. Grounding: the same note's
132:   adjudication (§Claims, anchor truth), Verify4, and `corpus/lessons/round-37.md`.
133: 
134: - **Q17 — a ratchet that equals the current debt is not a gate. The anchor floor is frozen,
135:   per anchor, and only shrinks.** A ceiling regenerated from the measured debt at landing
136:   certifies that debt. Round 37's `fidelity-ratchet.json` summed to exactly its `nonok` (200),
137:   so `FIDELITY: CLEAN` could not fail (`corpus/lessons/round-37-verifier-spotcheck.md`, §Claims
138:   and R2).
139:   - Anchor expectations live per anchor in `.ufo/pins/anchor-truth.json`.
140:   - The checklist runs `anchor-truth --base <frozen commit>`, so a note's debt may never rise
141:     and its `true` count may never fall against that floor.
142:   - A re-pin refuses any anchor that was true and is no longer true (`PIN_REGRESSION`).
143:   - Each such arm has a selftest fixture whose mutant must fail.
144:   - A repair is admitted only with zero true→false transitions against the round-open
145:     revision. The count is computed by the gate over both revisions and recorded with its
146:     command. Grounding: `corpus/lessons/round-38.md` (`## Mistakes` rows 1–2); S033 (a link is
147:     only stable against a commit id, never a moving head).
148: 
149: - **Q18 — lexical anchor truth is necessary, not semantic claim admission.** A definition
150:   token on a cited line does not prove a guarantee about its body, an error code, or a range
151:   covering both halves of a check. Read the body and the whole described assertion range.
152:   Grounding: round-38 falsifiers Check21 (cached preflight is not a network-never-needed
153:   guarantee; reap needs the age/lock/removal range), Check52 (uncoded Error, not a default
154:   typed code), and Check71 (tail-file readback lies one line past the cited range);
155:   `corpus/lessons/round-38.md`. The lexical gate must never be relabelled a prose oracle.
156: 
157: - **Q19 — a floor matches what it protects by an identity the protected change cannot edit.**
158:   Round 38's `--base` floor found each base-true anchor by its pin key, and the key is built
159:   from the paired token. A current pin that changed that entry's token and key, and dropped it
160:   to `unchecked`, escaped the per-anchor check while the per-note totals still passed
161:   (`corpus/lessons/round-38-verifier-spotcheck.md`, R38-1; round 39 ran it against the
162:   round-open gate: `FLOOR_PROBE accepted=6/6`, `.ufo/waves/round-39/final/floor-probe-open.txt`).
163:   - Identity for an anchor is its raw text, its resolved path and its occurrence index, never
164:     the token, the key or any other field the edit under test can rewrite.
165:   - Per raw text and path that held a true anchor at base, the count of non-true anchors may
166:     not grow, so an inserted true copy cannot mask the original.
167:   - A `pair` token must equal the note's own pairing, and an entry source is `pair` or
168:     `review:<seat>` with a token.
169:   - Each arm is admitted only with a fixture that fails on the old logic and a mutant that a
170:     test kills. A mutant that only crashes the run is a runtime error, not a kill (S034).
171:   Grounding: `corpus/lessons/round-39.md` (`## Mistakes` row 1); S034.
172: 
173: - **Q20 — a verdict guard is pinned by a selftest case, and the mutant that drops it is
174:   killed.** A gate's verdict expression is a set of guards; each guard must be the reason
175:   some named case reads the way it reads. A guard no case depends on is untested: the
176:   suite is green whether the guard is present or dropped, so the gate can report a
177:   verdict its own tests never checked.
178:   - Every term of a verdict expression (`filesScanned > 0`, `totals.resolved > 0`,
179:     `!drift`, and any term added later) must have a case whose asserted outcome changes
180:     when that term alone is removed.
181:   - The fix is shown able to fail before it counts. A claimed repair ships one red-before
182:     state in which the same command exits non-clean for the named reason, with the fix as
183:     the only delta, and the observed failure text is committed. A mutant that only crashes
184:     the run is a runtime error, not a kill (S034).
185:   - A case that asserts a verdict must assert it on the shape the guard protects: a
186:     scanned document with zero resolved citations and no drift is a different input from an
187:     empty scan set, and only the first exercises the `resolved` guard.
188:   - Grounding: R39-5, routed from the tameshi r26 closure
189:     (`tameshi-shokunin/corpus/lessons/round-26-verifier-spotcheck.md:172-179`);
190:     `corpus/lessons/round-39-verifier-spotcheck.md` R39-5. Measured at `f69817e`: dropping
191:     only `&& totals.resolved > 0` from `scripts/cite-check.mjs:1590` left the suite at
192:     `62/62 cases passed (hermetic)`, `VERDICT: PASS`, exit 0, while a scanned document with
193:     zero resolved citations and no drift read `VERDICT: FAIL` on the base and
194:     `VERDICT: PASS` under the mutant. With the round-40 fix in place the same mutant reads
195:     `63/64 cases passed (hermetic)`, `VERDICT: FAIL`, exit 1 — killed by the named
196:     zero-resolved case; the patched suite reads `64/64`, `VERDICT: PASS`, exit 0. One
197:     further mutant, `totals.filesScanned >= 0 && totals.resolved > 0 && !drift`, survives,
198:     and is an equivalent mutant of that expression: `resolved` only increments inside the
199:     per-document loop, so `resolved > 0` already implies `filesScanned > 0`. An equivalent
200:     mutant is a survivor, not a kill (S034), and it is recorded rather than hidden.
201:   - Round-40 falsify correction (seat CritQualityCriterion): the sentence above that "one
202:     further mutant … survives" is narrower than the sweep. Two more cite-check mutants survive
203:     the 64-case suite: dropping the `opts.strict && totals.warn > 0` part of `drift`, and
204:     dropping only `opts.strict &&` (no selftest passes `--strict`); and in
205:     `scripts/sources-check.mjs` forcing the JSON verdict to `CLEAN` passes 46/46. Each part of a
206:     compound term (here `drift`) is a term under this rule; these three are open and
207:     pre-registered for round 41.
