329: - **Q25 — a mutation battery has one kill predicate, frozen before any counted run and stated
330:   identically in the plan, the code and the selftest case names.** A predicate stated three ways is
331:   three predicates: the round is scored under the sentence the plan froze, and no artifact may state
332:   a narrower or wider rule beside it. Grounding: `corpus/lessons/round-42-verifier-spotcheck.md`
333:   §Claims C1 — plan `b237e3f0:.ufo/waves/round-42/plan.md:21-22` reads "killed = exit non-zero with a
334:   `VERDICT: FAIL` line", amendment A1 reads "at least one `FAIL ` case line", and the code at
335:   `c9a084bf:scripts/gate-mutants.mjs:426-434` reads `if (run.failLines > 0) return 'killed'`; under
336:   the frozen sentence the seven named survivors read `exit=0` or `VERDICT: PASS`. Also
337:   `corpus/lessons/round-42.md` `## Mistakes` row 3; routed defect D2.
338: 
339:   - **Who checks.** The lane L1 at plan commit, before any seat runs the counter; the non-author
340:     closure re-scores at least one clause from the committed receipt.
341:   - **Field.** (1) The plan states the predicate once, as `**K<nn> …**`, with clause letters `(a)`–`(d)`.
342:     (2) `scripts/gate-mutants.mjs` names the same `K<nn>` in its header. (3) Every case that asserts a
343:     predicate term carries the id as a lowercase prefix in its case id (`k<nn>-…`), and the plan
344:     carries one line per clause, `(x) case <case-id>`, naming that clause's binding case. (4) Each
345:     named case goes red when its clause alone is removed; the receipt is committed with the patch line
346:     quoted. (5) Nothing about the predicate changes after any seat or L1 has run the counter; a
347:     post-data change is an appended correction, and the counter is reported under the frozen text.
348:   - **Command.**
349:     ```sh
350:     N=43; P=$(grep -oE '^\*\*K[0-9]+' .ufo/waves/round-$N/plan.md | head -1 | tr -d '*'); p=$(printf '%s' "$P" | tr 'A-Z' 'a-z')
351:     sed -n '1,24p' scripts/gate-mutants.mjs | grep -c "$P"                       # header names the predicate
352:     grep -cE "check\('$p-[a-z0-9-]+'" scripts/gate-mutants.mjs                   # predicate cases, by id prefix
353:     grep -oE '\([a-d]\)' .ufo/waves/round-$N/plan.md | sort -u | wc -l            # clause count
354:     grep -cE "^\([a-d]\) case [a-z0-9-]+" .ufo/waves/round-$N/plan.md || true   # clause-to-case map, one per clause
355:     ```
356:     Clause binding is shown, not asserted: remove one clause from a copy of the gate inside a copy of
357:     `scripts/` (so the fixture siblings resolve) and run `--selftest`; the clean copy must read
358:     `GATE_MUTANTS_SELFTEST: 28/28 pass` exit 0, and each single-clause drop must read
359:     `27/28 pass`, `VERDICT: FAIL`, exit 1, with exactly one `FAIL k…` or named case line.
360:   - **Fails when.** Two artifacts state different predicates (round 42: three); a clause has no case
361:     that goes red when it is removed, or the receipt is absent; the predicate is edited after data and
362:     the round is scored under the edit; a predicate-asserting case carries no id prefix, or the plan
363:     carries no clause-to-case map.
364:   - **Measured at `e5ffcbe`.** Plan id `K43`; header mention count 2; seven `k43-…` case ids; four
365:     clause letters; clause-to-case map lines 0 (open arm). Clean selftest 28/28, exit 0. Single-clause
366:     drops: (a) `timeout-and-process-group-cleanup` fails, (b)
367:     `k43-exit-zero-with-verdict-fail-is-survived` fails, (c)
368:     `k43-nonzero-with-verdict-pass-is-survived` fails, (d)
369:     `k43-confirmation-other-names-or-pass-disagrees` fails; each 27/28, exit 1. The (a) binding case
370:     carries no `k43-` prefix, so the naming arm is also open.
