423:     ```sh
424:     d=$(mktemp); t=$(mktemp)
425:     find .ufo/waves/round-<N> -name '*.md' -printf '%P\n' | sort > "$d"
426:     git ls-files .ufo/waves/round-<N> | sed 's#^\.ufo/waves/round-<N>/##' | grep '\.md$' | sort > "$t"
427:     diff "$d" "$t"; rm -f "$d" "$t"                                               # prints nothing
428:     git status --porcelain --untracked-files=all -- .ufo/waves/round-<N>          # prints nothing
429:     git --no-optional-locks -C <fleet> status --porcelain --untracked-files=all -- .ufo/waves/round-<N> .ufo/reports/round-<N>
430:     ```
431:   - **Fails when.** Any `??` or `M` line under the wave directory at the report commit (round 42:
432:     three `??` falsify reports); the disk set and the tracked set differ; a report names a file whose
433:     bytes are not committed; a late delivery is argued as cancelled rather than committed and named.
434:   - **Measured at `e5ffcbe`.** Round 43 wave dir: status 0 lines; a planted
435:     `.ufo/waves/round-43/falsify/ProbeUntracked.md` produced exactly one `?? …` line, and removal
