439: - **Q28 — a knowledge section that a coverage term counts passes only if it cites a source row
440:   (unsourced-stub hole).** The admission unit for a knowledge note is its section, not its file: a
441:   section that names a declared member moves `K_sections` (and `coverage_kimi`) even when nothing in
442:   the section is sourced, so a stub can be counted as governance. Grounding:
443:   `corpus/lessons/round-42-verifier-spotcheck.md` §Routed defects D7 ("an unsourced stub section
444:   passes every C2 counter (CritC2Claim objections 3–5)"; "S041 binding is a manual grep") and
445:   `corpus/lessons/round-42.md` `## Open limits` (same sentence). The base exemption takes Q19's
446:   identity rule: identity is (file, heading text, occurrence index), and the count at base may not
447:   grow, so a duplicate heading cannot mask a new one.
448: 
449:   - **Who checks.** The seat that adds or retitles a section; the lane L1 before the report commit;
450:     the non-author closure re-runs the scan and the blindness probe.
451:   - **Field.** A counted section is a `##` heading in `corpus/knowledge/kimi-*.md` that names a K
452:     member (`K_sections` unit; same heading-binding rule as the `K_sections` derivation in
453:     `scripts/proxy-check.mjs`, whose ambiguous case is the `K_SECTION_AMBIGUOUS` warning).
454:     Base `16a5441` fixes the exempt count per (file, heading text). An occurrence beyond the base
455:     count is new and passes only if, inside its own bounds, it cites at least one `S###` whose
456:     `corpus/SOURCES.md` row reads `status=mined` and names this file in `used-by`; otherwise the
457:     section reads `K_SECTION_UNSOURCED`, is excluded from `K_sections`, and cannot raise a coverage
458:     term. Readme rows and file counts are not section evidence.
459:   - **Command.**
460:     ```sh
461:     IDS=$(sed -n '/const K_MEMBER_RULES/,/^];/p' scripts/proxy-check.mjs | grep -oE "path: '[^']+'" | cut -d"'" -f2)
462:     # base heading counts per file; print each occurrence beyond base with no S### inside its bounds
463:     for f in corpus/knowledge/kimi-*.md; do b=$(mktemp); git show 16a5441:"$f" 2>/dev/null | grep '^## ' > "$b"; \
464:       awk -v F="$f" -v B="$b" -v IDS="$IDS" '
465:         BEGIN{nid=split(IDS,ids,"\n");while((getline l < B)>0)base[l]++}
466:         /^## /{if(sec!=""&&newsec&&nc==0)print F":"ln": "sec;sec=$0;ln=FNR;nc=0;binds=0;
467:                for(i=1;i<=nid;i++)if(ids[i]!=""&&index(sec,ids[i])){binds=1;break};
468:                seen[sec]++;newsec=binds&&(seen[sec]>base[sec]);next}
469:         /S[0-9][0-9][0-9]/{nc++}
470:         END{if(sec!=""&&newsec&&nc==0)print F":"ln": "sec}' "$f"; rm -f "$b"; done   # prints nothing
471:     awk -F'|' '$2 ~ /^ *S041 *$/{s=$9;u=$12;gsub(/^ +| +$/,"",s);gsub(/^ +| +$/,"",u);print s, u}' corpus/SOURCES.md
472:     ```
473:   - **Fails when.** A new counted section cites nothing (measured: one); the cited id is `rejected`,
474:     unknown, or its row does not name the file; the counter counts an uncited section (measured: the
475:     stripped-citation probe leaves `K_sections` unchanged).
476:   - **Measured at `e5ffcbe`.** Scan prints one line:
477:     ``corpus/knowledge/kimi-skills-plugins.md:173: ## `~/.kimi-code/skills/cursor-lane` `` (base file
478:     has 13 headings; this heading is absent at base). The round-42 `locks/` section passes: `S041
479:     status=mined` and its `used-by` names `corpus/knowledge/kimi-session-state.md`. Hole still open at
480:     the gate: deleting `S041`/`S042` from inside that section in a scratch copy leaves
481:     `K_sections=53 coverage_kimi=10` and `SOURCES_CHECK: CLEAN (rows=45 … legacy=38)`.
