483: - **Q29 — an operability counter must reject named skip-work controls before data.** A counter that passes
484:   only because a control skips the claimed work is not evidence; round 43's junk J4 returned
485:   `GATE_MUTANTS: CLEAN` with synthetic failures (`.ufo/waves/round-43/build/ExecJunkControls.md:22-29`;
486:   `corpus/lessons/round-43.md`, `## Mistakes` and `## Open limits`).
487:   - **Who checks.** The L1 before the first data run; the non-author closure replays the committed receipts.
488:   - **Field.** The frozen plan names absent, constant, junk, no-reader and label-keyed shortcut controls. Each runs
489:     against the frozen counter before data; its receipt names the control and counter revision and is committed
490:     before the measured receipt. Any control returning the counter's success verdict requires redesign before data
491:     or an explicit exploratory claim; no data run under the old counter supports the claim.
492:   - **Command.**
493:     ```sh
494:     L=...; P=<plan commit>; C=<control-receipt commit>; R=<measured-receipt commit>
495:     F=(<committed control receipt paths>)
496:     git -C "$L" log --format='%H %s' --ancestry-path --reverse "$P^..$R"
497:     if ! git -C "$L" merge-base --is-ancestor "$P" "$C" || ! git -C "$L" merge-base --is-ancestor "$C" "$R"; then
498:       echo 'Q29: FAIL plan/control/measured commits are out of order'; exit 1
499:     fi
500:     for f in "${F[@]}"; do git -C "$L" cat-file -e "$C:$f" || exit 1; done
501:     if git -C "$L" grep -n -E '[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]*: (MET|CLEAN)' "$C" -- "${F[@]}"; then
502:       echo 'Q29: FAIL a control met the counter'; exit 1
503:     fi
504:     ```
505:     The log must order plan → controls → measured; the final grep must print nothing. `CLEAN` is included to
506:     recognize round 43's positive token; round 44 uses `MET`.
507:   - **Fails when.** A named control is omitted, a receipt is absent or committed after measurement, or any
508:     control produces the success verdict; a hit requires redesign before data or an explicit exploratory claim.
509:   - **Demonstrated at round 43.** The J4 receipt commit `fb3eab40` precedes measured `84cb1d5d`; its `CLEAN`
510:     line makes this check exit 1 (`.ufo/waves/round-43/build/ExecJunkControls.md:26`).
511: 
512: - **Q29 ordering note (round 45, routed defect R44-2).** The round-44 closure asked for control receipts "in a commit
513:   earlier than the counter they score, not in the same one". A receipt that scores frozen counter bytes cannot
514:   precede the counter's freeze commit, so the field reads: each control receipt lands in its **own** commit, a
515:   descendant of the counter's freeze commit and an ancestor of the measured receipt, and never in the counter's
516:   freeze commit. Round 44's receipts shared `32b7fd56` with p44d; that fails this note (recorded, not re-judged).
517:   Add to the Q29 command, with `K=<counter path>` (the line exits 1 when the receipt commit also last touched the
518:   counter):
519:   ```sh
520:   test "$(git -C "$L" log -1 --format=%H "$C" -- "$K")" != "$C" || { echo 'Q29: FAIL receipts share the counter commit'; exit 1; }
521:   ```
522:   On round 44 (`C=32b7fd56`, `K=.ufo/waves/round-44/probe/p44d-count.mjs`) it prints the FAIL line. (A draft of this
523:   note read `git log -1` without `"$C"` and ended in `|| echo`, so it measured HEAD and never exited 1 — round-45
524:   seat ScoutErrataCheck item 3.)
