615: - **Round-45 attempt-3 replay notes on Q30–Q32 (history replays in wave `a3-falsify`; the criteria above are not
616:   reworded).**
617:   - **Q30 — fixed CLEAN cases always recur (ReplayQ30History).** Run as written on the round-44 counters, p44
618:     (`361d4492`) and p44b (`292d9266`) exit 2 (their CLI has no `--seed`, and without it the listing cannot be rebuilt:
619:     `reconstructed 38 entries, listing says 39`); p44c (`28e29bbe`) reads `CATALOG: REUSED (clean=19 recurring=9)`,
620:     exit 1. The nine recurring ids are the seed-independent fixed shapes (`control`, `control-end`, `no-chains`,
621:     `no-sidecars`, five `src:*`), and an alternate seed pair returns the same nine. So any counter with one fixed CLEAN
622:     case (an unmodified root, a sourced reference shape) reads `REUSED` whatever its other cases do: as written Q30
623:     cannot pass a counter that keeps a do-nothing CLEAN case. Reading from round 46, until the script gains an
624:     allow-list: the frozen plan names its fixed CLEAN case ids before the run; `REUSED` passes only when every recurring
625:     id is in that list and the non-fixed CLEAN cases number at least the counter's floor; any other recurring id fails.
626:     That reading is checked by hand against the script's printed ids.
627:   - **Q31 — the source greps are blind out of sample (Q31OutOfSample).** On 34 real launchers (lane scripts, round
628:     probes, tameshi runners) the four greps gave 11 false passes and 3 false fails; a mutant that spreads
629:     `...process.env` into `claims-check.mjs`'s child environment survived the environment grep while a behavioural
630:     marker probe caught it (`ENV_BUILDER: FAIL MARKER present`). The selftest clause of **Fails when** is the criterion;
631:     the greps are a reminder list and never pass or fail a runner on their own.
632:   - **Q32 — replay agrees (ReplayQ32History).** Over the 22 round boundaries of rounds 35–45 every base fails with
633:     exactly the previous round's `round-<N-1>-verifier-spotcheck.md` and every tip passes; against the eight recorded
634:     round-open proxy receipts, 0 false negatives and 0 false positives; over 96 commits Q32 fails at exactly the 31
635:     where declared and computed `C2_total` differ. Limits: Q32 checks that a row exists, not that the declared total
636:     matches (a declared-only drift passes Q32), and it does not detect phantom or duplicate rows (a row whose note no longer exists); a note renamed with its row
637:     left behind does fail Q32 while the proxy reads MATCH.
638:   - **Revision after residual review (RevQualityNotes; the bullets above stay as written).** (1) The Q30 fixed-case
639:     reading above is gameable: declaring every CLEAN case "fixed" satisfies it, and "the counter's floor" is defined
640:     nowhere in this file. Bounded reading from round 46: at most **two** fixed CLEAN ids, each named in the frozen plan
641:     with the reason it cannot vary (an unmodified root, one sourced reference shape); at least **20** non-fixed CLEAN
642:     cases (round 44's case floor); any recurring id outside the named pair fails; the junk-variation control of the
643:     Field still has to read the counter's failure verdict. (2) The Q31 sentence "never pass or fail a runner on their
644:     own" narrowed **Fails when**: a printed guard line still fails the runner as Q31 states; the greps never pass a
645:     runner without the behavioural selftest, and the three false fails above are recorded so a runner can avoid those
646:     spellings (shell `env -i`, Python `env=`, a multiline `process.once` loop).
