648: Q33–Q34 and the frozen-checklist rule were added in round 46 (routed defects D2 and D4 of
649: `corpus/lessons/round-45-verifier-spotcheck.md` § 5) and are in force from round 47. Drafts: scribe ScribeQuality;
650: commands and their fail/pass runs: executor ExecQualityFailCmds (`.ufo/waves/round-46/build/`).
651: 
652: - **Q33 — a SOURCES row's `teaches` is checked against every locator in its anchor cell before the entry commit.**
653:   Grounding: the K3′ ruling on S073 and D2 (`corpus/lessons/round-45-verifier-spotcheck.md:61-71,123-125`).
654:   - **Who checks.** The entry author checks every locator before committing the entry. A non-author re-opens every
655:     row's quote and `teaches` cell before the freeze (round 46 did this for all 77 rows: the `Sweep*` receipts in
656:     `.ufo/waves/round-46/build/`).
657:   - **Field.** Open every locator in the anchor cell. Check each clause of the `teaches` cell against the located
658:     bytes, and record which locator supports it. Narrow or split an unsupported clause before the commit. One locator
659:     never stands in for another.
660:   - **Command** (a tripwire over committed check lines; it proves a check was recorded, not that it was right):
661:     ```sh
662:     .ufo/waves/round-46/quality/q33-locator-coverage.sh <lane> <rev> corpus/lessons/round-<N>.md
663:     ```
664:     For each row admitted in the lesson's `## Gate`, every anchor locator must be co-named with the row id in a
665:     committed check line (the lesson or a `.ufo/**/*.md` receipt). `Q33 FAIL`, exit 1, on any uncovered locator.
666:   - **Fails when.** The command prints `Q33 UNCOVERED`; or a re-open finds a clause that no locator states.
667:   - **Shown able to fail.** At `6b2a4517` with `corpus/lessons/round-45.md`: `Q33 UNCOVERED S073
668:     anchor-locators-checked=1/4 missing=[buffer.html,getrlimit,prlimit]` (also S068 1/5, S072 2/3), exit 1; on a
669:     fixture where both locators of one row are checked: `Q33 COVERED S901 locators=2/2`, exit 0.
670:   - **Limit.** The locator tokenizer is heuristic: an anchor that names only sections yields zero locators and passes
671:     trivially, so the re-open half of **Fails when** carries those rows.
672: 
673: - **Q34 — a guard prescribed in an entry or a wave context is byte-identical to the guard in the receipt that
674:   tested it.** Grounding: D4 and erratum X4 (`corpus/lessons/round-45-verifier-spotcheck.md:38-43,128-130`;
675:   `.ufo/waves/round-45/a3-falsify/AblScrubRow.md`).
676:   - **Who checks.** The author copies the tested bytes and cites the receipt. A non-author compares the two before
677:     the freeze.
678:   - **Field.** Copy the whole tested guard, quoting, redirections and wrapper arguments included. If any byte changes,
679:     re-test the changed guard and cite the new receipt.
680:   - **Command.**
681:     ```sh
682:     .ufo/waves/round-46/quality/q34-guard-bytecmp.sh <entry-file> <row-ere> <receipt-file> [guard-ere]
683:     ```
684:     Prescribed = the longest backtick span on the matched table row; tested = the first fenced-block line of the
685:     receipt matching the guard pattern; `cmp`. `Q34 FAIL`, exit 1, on any difference.
686:   - **Fails when.** `Q34 MISMATCH`; no receipt is cited; the cited receipt does not contain the guard.
687:   - **Shown able to fail.** Entry row 3 at `6b2a4517` against the receipt `SentinelSeatEnvScrub.md`:
688:     `Q34 MISMATCH … (212B) vs (306B)`, differing at byte 3, exit 1; a fixture with the same 54-byte guard on both sides:
689:     `Q34 IDENTICAL`, exit 0.
690:   - **Limit.** One span per row: a row that prescribes two guards needs one run per guard.
691: 
692: - **Frozen-checklist rule (D2).** Every item of a frozen claim checklist states, before the freeze, whether an
693:   appended erratum can cure its failure, and if so what qualifies. An item that states nothing is not curable. A later
694:   correction never changes an item's frozen failure, and no item borrows another item's erratum clause. Round 46 has
695:   no prose checklist: both obligations of its claim are counters (`.ufo/waves/round-46/plan.md` § A2/A3), and their
696:   kill rule admits no erratum.
