698: Q35 was added in round 47 (routed defect R46-1 of `corpus/lessons/round-46-verifier-spotcheck.md`).
699: 
700: - **Q35 — an existing `SOURCES.md` row is append-only except for `status`, `recheck` and `used-by`.** Grounding: fleet
701:   `CORPUS.md:116-118` Rule 2 and R46-1: round 46 rewrote 13 existing rows in place without `supersedes` rows.
702:   - **Who checks.** The author runs the comparison from the revision before the round's first registry edit to the
703:     candidate before committing a correction. A non-author checks the same receipt at close and confirms that each
704:     correction is a new row whose `teaches` opens `supersedes S0NN —`.
705:   - **Field.** For every registry id present at base, the cells `id`, `source`, `kind`, `tier`, `scope`, `anchor`,
706:     `teaches` and `opened` stay byte-identical at tip (padding trimmed); a removed base row also fails. Only `status`,
707:     `recheck` and `used-by` may change in place.
708:   - **Command.**
709:     ```sh
710:     .ufo/waves/round-47/quality/q35-append-only.sh <lane> <base-rev> <tip-rev>
711:     ```
712:     It reads committed `corpus/SOURCES.md` at both revisions and prints `Q35 rewritten=<n> removed=<m>` plus one line
713:     per offending id; exit 1 when n+m>0, 0 when clean, 2 on usage or Git errors.
714:   - **Fails when.** Any frozen cell differs or a base row is removed; no receipt is cited.
715:   - **Shown able to fail.** `2b2bf7bb 9b33e03e` → `Q35 rewritten=13 removed=0` (S003, S004, S013, S041, S047,
716:     S051–S055, S061, S073, S076), exit 1; sandbox fixtures: a `teaches` edit and an `opened` edit exit 1, a row removal
717:     exits 1, a `used-by` edit, an appended `supersedes` row and padding only exit 0
718:     (`.ufo/waves/round-47/build/ExecQ35AppendOnly.md`).
719:   - **Limit.** Committed revisions only, keyed by id; it does not judge whether a `supersedes` row is correct — the
720:     non-author re-open does. A restoration of rewritten rows (round 47) reads as rewritten against the revision that
721:     carried the rewrite; run it against the revision before the rewrite (`2b2bf7bb` for round 46's).
722: - **Q36 (round 48, 2026-10-23; amended wording per `r48/ReviewQualityDraft.md`).** A frozen-counter success verdict is scoreable only with N≥2 committed receipts for the same frozen command/revision, every run exit 0 with byte-identical success summaries, complete trace parsing/pairing, and per-site counts equal to the plan-pinned base counts; otherwise no success verdict is scoreable. Command: the receipt pair is re-derived by re-running the frozen command; shown able to fail: the r47 A2 re-runs at f00cf278 (`r48/ScribeReceipts-a2-rerun-{1,2,3}.txt`, 3/5, 3/5, 4/5) score nothing.
723: - **Q37 (round 48, 2026-10-23).** Wave-seat receipts are claims until the L1 recomputes their bytes: the L1-owned manifest `.ufo/waves/round-48/r48/L1-receipts.sha256` binds every wave/close receipt at integration; 0-byte or trailer-less receipts count as claims only (SentinelReceipt; the 0-byte class observed live by MutRunnerLooseMem).
