727: - **Q38 — a knowledge entry's clause is bound to a committed receipt by content hash, and the entry scores only when a
728:   frozen probe verifies every binding at the scored revision.** Grounding: the round-48 discipline lived in
729:   round-scoped receipts and scorecard prose; `corpus/knowledge/counter-amendment-discipline.md` states it as clauses
730:   whose evidence is a sha256 token.
731:   - **Who checks.** The author writes each clause with a `receipt:<repo-path>@sha256:<64 hex>` token computed from the
732:     committed blob; the C2 probe verifies all of them at the scored revision, and a non-author re-reads the prose
733:     against the receipts.
734:   - **Field.** One token per clause line; the token names a path under a frozen round directory (never the lane's
735:     moving documents, whose hash changes at the next edit).
736:   - **Command.**
737:     ```sh
738:     node .ufo/waves/round-49/probe/doctrine49-probe.mjs <lane> <rev> [--file <entry>]
739:     ```
740:     It prints `DOCTRINE49: HELD clauses=<n>/<n> rows=<m> entry_sha256=<sha>` exit 0, or `DOCTRINE49: UNMET reason=…`
741:     exit 1; floors `clauses>=10`, `rows>=2` with status `mined`; exit 2 on an unreadable revision.
742:   - **Fails when.** Any token's hash differs or its path is absent; any cited row is not `mined`; the clause or row
743:     floor is missed.
744:   - **Shown able to fail.** At `589d25e4` the entry reads `HELD clauses=15/15 rows=3` exit 0; the same entry with one
745:     hex digit changed reads `UNMET reason=receipts misses=.ufo/waves/round-48/plan.md=hash-mismatch(6faa34ab!=6faa34ab)`
746:     exit 1 (`.ufo/waves/round-49/r49/C2-doctored-control-589d25e4*.txt`).
747:   - **Limit.** The probe checks binding, not truth: a well-bound false clause passes, and the non-author re-read
748:     carries that half. `--file` verifies a worktree entry against a revision's receipts, so it is a control mode, not
749:     a scoring mode.
