754: - **Q39 — a claim of time-spaced re-runs needs a distinct, captured invocation receipt for each run.**
755:   Grounding: the three round-49 C1 receipts have one sha256 (`corpus/lessons/round-49-verifier-spotcheck.md:63-66`),
756:   so their bytes do not establish the report's “three time-spaced runs”.
757:   - **Who checks.** The author records the UTC start time, exact command, output and exit code in each
758:     separate receipt. The non-author compares hashes and re-derives the timestamp span from those receipts.
759:   - **Field.** Each receipt begins with `run-at=<ISO-8601 UTC>`; hashes must be distinct and the elapsed span
760:     must meet the round's pre-registered minimum. Identical output-only receipts do not establish
761:     independent invocations; genuine deterministic runs can emit identical output.
762:   - **Command.** `node .ufo/waves/round-50/probe/repairs50-probe.mjs <lane> <rev> --fleet <fleet>` (R4).
763:   - **Fails when.** A timestamp is absent/unparseable, any bytes repeat, any run fails, or the measured span
764:     is below the frozen minimum.
765:   - **Shown able to fail.** Round-49 `sha256sum r49/L1-score-0526f898.txt r49/ReRunCounter49-2.txt
766:     r49/ReRunCounter49-3.txt` → `03a258d6…` ×3; the round-50 control is `R4 MISS files=0`
767:     (`.ufo/waves/round-50/controls/CtlR50-base-ff40d7d-r2.txt`).
768:   - **Limit.** `run-at` is captured evidence, not a cryptographic timestamp, and `CritB49CounterAttack`
769:     executed this frozen R4 block in memory over one old deterministic body with three rewritten preludes:
770:     `PASS files=3 distinct=3 held=3 span_s=600`, `body_distinct=1` — a prelude-only replay satisfies R4.
771:     The receipts are author-attested invocation records; defeating a forger needs a separately frozen
772:     captured-invocation design, not a text check.
773: 
774: - **Q40 — a runner must not rebind a sandbox-managed mount root, explicitly or through its implicit cwd bind.**
775:   Grounding: S095 says filesystem actions apply in argument order; `ScoutCapRunVisibility` found that
776:   `--bind /tmp /tmp` after `--tmpfs /tmp` re-exposes host `/tmp`, and `LabratSystemd` reproduced the same
777:   escape through cap-run's automatic `--bind cwd cwd` when cwd was `/tmp` (`corpus/lessons/round-50.md` M4).
778:   - **Who checks.** The author guards both the parsed bind and the implicit cwd path; the hermetic suite checks
779:     both surfaces, and the L1 re-runs G50 at the committed candidate.
780:   - **Field.** Explicit whole-root binds and cwd resolved to `/`, `/tmp`, `/proc`, `/sys`, `/dev` or `/run`
781:     exit 64 before a child runs; a bind of a real subdirectory under `/tmp` still works.
782:   - **Command.** `node scripts/cap-run.mjs --selftest`; `node .ufo/waves/round-50/probe/bindguard50-probe.mjs <lane> <rev>` (G2/G3/G4).
783:   - **Fails when.** Any protected root reaches the child, a legal `/tmp` subdirectory bind is refused, or G50
784:     is not `GUARD_HELD`.
785:   - **Shown able to fail.** The pre-guard child wrote `/tmp/r50-host-tmp-exposed` through `--bind /tmp`
786:     (`.ufo/waves/round-50/controls/CtlExposure-base-ff40d7d.txt`); `LabratSystemd.md` reproduced a host write
787:     from cwd `/tmp`; base G50 read `GUARD_UNMET held=5/8` (`CtlG50-base-ff40d7d-r1.txt`).
788:   - **Limit.** This guards cap-run's own API, not direct bwrap callers.
789: 
790: - **Q41 — every gate-count sentence in the SKILL registry is reconciled against the `kind=gate` rows.**
791:   Grounding: the r49 non-author closure found `Twelve are gates` beside two stale “all eleven” sentences
792:   (`corpus/lessons/round-49-verifier-spotcheck.md:144-145`).
793:   - **Who checks.** The author counts the registry's `gate` rows and searches every prose count in the same
794:     section; a non-author compares the count and the full search output before closure.
795:   - **Field.** `grep -c '| gate |' SKILL.md` is the row count; `grep -iEn 'eleven|twelve|[0-9]+ gates?' SKILL.md`
796:     enumerates the count assertions, case-insensitively, for comparison.
797:   - **Fails when.** A count differs from the registry rows or any stale occurrence survives the sweep.
798:   - **Shown able to fail.** At r49 open, the registry said Twelve while `SKILL.md:595` and `:598` each said
799:     “all eleven”; the exact conflicting lines are in the verifier-spotcheck artifact above.
800:   - **Limit.** The text sweep is scoped to `SKILL.md`; it does not discover count claims in other documents.
801: - **Q43 — a frozen counter is not frozen until it has been executed, and its declared
802:   controls must be executed against it.**
803:   Classes caught: unrun-check (A51 v1 could not parse; D51 v1 unsatisfiable — both found
804:   by seats within minutes of wave 1), vacuous kill rule (the plan's "a stub cannot clear
805:   A1/A3" fell to a print-stub; the full-tree forger scored held=5/5).
806:   Fix: at freeze time the L1 runs the counter at base and commits the receipt
807:   (`base/attest-base-v3r6.txt`, `held=0/9`); every freeze repair re-runs it; every declared
808:   do-nothing control is executed by a seat before data, not asserted. From round 51 on, a
809:   counter whose before-state receipt is absent from the freeze commit is a conformance
810:   defect, not a predicate.
811:   - **Fails when.** A freeze commit lacks the executed before-receipt, or a declared
812:     control was never run.
813:   - **Shown able to fail.** The round-51 wave-1 seats: two independent findings for D51's
814:     index bug; CritC1's stub reading; RevCounterA's held=5/5 forger.
815:   - **Limit.** The rule binds the L1's freeze discipline; it does not make static arms
816:     unforgeable (see round-51 report, forgery boundary). Enforcement is MANUAL — the L1
817:     commits the before-receipt at freeze and the non-author closure verifies it; no lane
818:     gate mechanically rejects a freeze commit that lacks one (seat CritQ43, round 51).
819: - **Q44 — a round's FINAL claim receipt must be executed against the measured close
820:   revision it cites, and the receipt commit must carry an idempotence re-run.**
821:   Classes caught: receipt-rev ≠ cited-rev (R52-11: round-51's FINAL receipt cites
822:   `57333ead`, was committed at `cb6c472` — one commit after the measured close rev
823:   `fef67079` and two after the rev it cites — and no A51/D51 receipt exists at
824:   `fef67079`, so the 9/9 filed there was compositional); compositional citation
825:   masquerading as measured (the same 655-byte FINAL file joins a rev-bound `held=8/9`
826:   line whose A5 records `PROXY: DRIFT … declared=81 computed=71` with an un-rev-bound
827:   `PROXY: MATCH (A=81 …)` line — at the rev it names `SCORECARD.md` declares A=81
828:   against a computed 71, and at `fef67079` it declares A=71, so no committed tree
829:   yields that MATCH [INFERENCE: the transient seat scratch named by commit `fef6707`]).
830:   Fix: the R52-11 close sequence (round-52 plan `## Close sequence`). R1 is the
831:   integration tip; A52 and D52 run against R1 and both receipts are committed as
832:   `close/FINAL-<R1>.txt`. R2 is that receipt commit; both counters re-run against R2
833:   and the transcript is committed as `close/IDEMPOTENCE-<R2>.txt` (R3). The report and
834:   SCORECARD cite measured close revision R1, name R2/R3 as the receipt/idempotence
835:   commits, and quote the committed FINAL verdict line verbatim — the cited rev and the
836:   receipt rev are the same tree by construction, and the tip carries a re-run against
837:   its own bytes.
838:   - **Fails when.** The FINAL verdict's `rev=` is not the cited close revision; no
839:     receipt file exists at the cited rev; one transcript mixes lines from different
840:     tree states (an un-rev-bound line, or a line contradicting the stanza declared at
841:     the rev it names); the receipt commit carries no idempotence transcript; a FINAL
842:     line is re-wrapped or truncated mid-token.
843:   - **Shown able to fail.** Round-51's own FINAL receipt:
844:     `.ufo/waves/round-51/close/FINAL-57333ead13b1b39419bdb1cf6502fad0aa8523ff.txt`
845:     (`sha256 0c1f9b22…`, 6 lines / 655 bytes) reads
846:     `ATTEST51: ATTEST_UNMET held=8/9 … rev=57333ead…` and was added by `cb6c472`.
847:     `grep -rn 'rev=fef67079' .ufo/waves/round-51` prints nothing and
848:     `find .ufo/waves/round-51 -iname '*idempot*'` prints nothing; its line 1 is 280
849:     bytes and ends mid-word at `delt`. The spotcheck files the route itself
850:     (`corpus/lessons/round-51-verifier-spotcheck.md:71`).
851:   - **Limit.** `rev=` is a self-declared field: this binds rev identity, file presence
852:     and transcript consistency, not byte provenance, and a forger who writes a
853:     receipt-shaped file naming the right rev still passes (the r49 forgery boundary);
854:     only a probe-emitted digest-bound receipt (A52's B2 arm class) narrows that.
855:     Enforcement is MANUAL — the L1 runs both counters at R1, commits FINAL and
856:     IDEMPOTENCE, and the non-author closure compares cited rev to receipt rev and the
857:     receipt commit to the transcript; no lane gate mechanically rejects a close commit
858:     whose FINAL receipt cites another revision (seat ScribeQuality, round 52).
859: 
860: - **Q45 — a pending non-author spot-check pointer is closed by an append-only named correction when its separate artifact lands.** Grounding: `corpus/lessons/round-53.md`'s `## Gate` still said `<pending>` after the non-author re-open had landed separately in `corpus/lessons/round-53-verifier-spotcheck.md` §3 (R53-1 in this round's `corpus/lessons/round-54.md`).
861:   - **Who checks.** In the next lane round, the author appends a correction naming the committed spot-check artifact and its verdict; the non-author confirms that both the pointer and the verdict resolve. The original pending line stays unchanged.
862:   - **Field.** One appended `## Gate correction (round N)` section names the artifact, section, sampled admits/rejects and `AGREE`/`DISAGREE` with reason; it never rewrites the old `## Gate` text.
863:   - **Command.** `grep -nE 'round-53-verifier-spotcheck\.md.*AGREE|AGREE.*round-53-verifier-spotcheck\.md' corpus/lessons/round-53.md` → the appended correction line.
864:   - **Fails when.** At the round-53 base `383ad787`, `grep -n '<pending' corpus/lessons/round-53.md` finds the open marker while `grep -n 'round-53-verifier-spotcheck.md' corpus/lessons/round-53.md` finds nothing, despite the separate check artifact; the correction is still required even when the reviewer artifact already exists.
865:   - **Shown able to fail.** Base `383ad787`: the Gate line is `<pending>` and the pointer sweep is empty; this round appends the round-54 Gate correction pointing at the non-author §3 source re-open, without changing the old line.
866:   - **Limit.** The command checks the durable pointer and verdict text, not whether the named reviewer actually re-opened the evidence; the non-author re-reads the cited artifact.
867: 
868: - **Q46 — an opened SOURCES row is bound to committed capture bytes (or an explicit exemption); a URL alone is not a resolvable location at closure.** Grounding: `corpus/lessons/round-54-verifier-spotcheck.md` §5 item 1 (routed defect R54-C1): S108's reject rested on bytes that were never committed, so a non-author could not re-open the adjudicated evidence.
869:   - **Who checks.** The `source-capture` gate (`node scripts/source-capture.mjs`, contract `kumitate-source-capture-v1`) verifies it mechanically: every `S###` row in `corpus/SOURCES.md` must resolve to exactly one binding — a `.ufo/pins/source-captures.json` capture (committed bytes + sha256 + byte size + capture date) or an exemption naming the reason — and no binding may name a row that does not exist.
870:   - **Command.** `node scripts/source-capture.mjs` → exit 0 + `SOURCE_CAPTURE: CLEAN captures=<n> exemptions=<m>`; `node scripts/source-capture.mjs --selftest` → `SOURCE_CAPTURE_SELFTEST: PASS (13/13)`.
871:   - **Fails when.** Any S### row is uncaptured and unexempted; a capture's bytes are absent, symlinked, hash- or size-mismatched, or escape the registry base; a binding names a row that does not exist; the registry is malformed (duplicate sourceId, capture+exemption conflict, version ≠ 1) — the last is FAIL-CLOSED, could-not-evaluate, never CLEAN.
872:   - **Shown able to fail.** At base `c562d28` the registry and gate did not exist and `node scripts/source-capture.mjs` exited non-zero; the gate's 13-case hermetic selftest fires each drift arm (capture-absent, hash-mismatch, not-a-regular-file, bytes-mismatch, path-escape, uncaptured, orphan-capture, captures-empty) and each fail-closed arm (malformed/version/dup/conflict/unreadable-sources) once.
873:   - **Limit.** The gate binds bytes and identity, not truth: a committed capture could still mis-quote the source (the non-author re-read carries that half); pre-rule rows S001–S107 are exempt by declaration, not proof their bytes were ever read.
874: 
875: - **Q47 — a SOURCES duplicate-URL group exists only as a pinned `known` entry.** Grounding: the maintained census (`scripts/sources-census.sh validate`) reports W04 same-URL-across-scopes as a *warning* that never gates, so the lane's registry drifted to four live duplicate groups (S023+S034, S047+S084, S060+S068, S069+S095) — each a source admitted twice under different scopes, splitting which row is authoritative. Routed-adjacent class of R55-V2 (a number or set the lane asserts must be re-derived over committed bytes, and the assertion itself must become mechanical where it recurs).
876:   - **Who checks.** The `source-dupes` gate (`node scripts/source-dupes.mjs`, contract `kumitate-source-dupes-v1`) verifies it mechanically: the live duplicate-group set computed over `corpus/SOURCES.md` Registry rows must equal the pinned `known` set in `.ufo/pins/source-dupes.json` — new group = DRIFT `new-duplicate`, resolved group = DRIFT `stale-known` until its pin is removed, member/url shape mismatch = DRIFT `known-mismatch`, malformed pin set = FAIL-CLOSED.
877:   - **Command.** `node scripts/source-dupes.mjs` → exit 0 + `SOURCE_DUPES: CLEAN groups=<n> known=<n>`; `node scripts/source-dupes.mjs --selftest` → `SOURCE_DUPES_SELFTEST: PASS (12/12)`.
878:   - **Fails when.** A new `S###` row re-uses an already-registered URL under a different scope; a pinned group's members are edited so it stops duplicating without the pin being retired; a `known` entry's ids/url do not match the live group it covers; the registry is malformed, version ≠ 1, or a row id is covered by two pins.
879:   - **Shown able to fail.** The gate's 12-case hermetic selftest fires each arm (new-duplicate, stale-known, known-mismatch, known-url-mismatch, empty-known-with-live-dup, empty-clean, normalization parity, malformed JSON, version ≠ 1, overlapping pins, sources absent). Live: at round-56 open the census printed exactly the four pinned W04 groups and `node scripts/source-dupes.mjs` reads `CLEAN groups=4 known=4`.
880:   - **Limit.** The gate pins the *set*, not the rightness of keeping a duplicate: resolving a pinned group is deliberate lane work (supersede or re-anchor one row, then remove the pin) — the gate enforces that the resolution is visible, not that it happens fast.
881: 
882: - **Q48 — a corpus file lands only with its `corpus/README.md` map row and its `covered` pin, in the same change.** Grounding: `corpus/lessons/round-56-verifier-spotcheck.md` §6 routed defect R56-V3 — the third recurrence (r52, r55, r56 verifier spotchecks) of a corpus file landing post-close without a coverage-map row; the count-only C2 term in `proxy-check` caught the drift one count at a time and could not name WHICH file lacked a row.
883:   - **Who checks.** The `readme-map` gate (`node scripts/readme-map.mjs`, contract `kumitate-readme-map-v1`) verifies it mechanically: the live bimap over `corpus/knowledge` + `corpus/lessons` must satisfy three conjuncts — every `*.md` carries exactly one `| `path` |` README row, every such row names a live file, and every live file is pinned in `.ufo/pins/readme-map.json`'s `covered` set; `uncovered` / `orphan-row` / `duplicate-row` / `format-unmapped` / `stale-covered` / `unpinned` are DRIFT, a malformed registry/README/corpus-dir is FAIL-CLOSED.
884:   - **Command.** `node scripts/readme-map.mjs` → exit 0 + `README_MAP: CLEAN files=<n> rows=<n> covered=<n>`; `node scripts/readme-map.mjs --selftest` → `README_MAP_SELFTEST: PASS (14/14)`.
885:   - **Fails when.** A corpus file lands without a row or a pin; a row names a deleted file; a path is double-mapped; a covered file loses its row or disappears; the registry is malformed, version ≠ 1, or a covered entry leaves the `knowledge|lessons` namespace.
886:   - **Shown able to fail.** The gate's 14-case hermetic selftest fires each arm (clean, uncovered, orphan-row, duplicate-row, format-unmapped, stale-covered, unpinned, empty-covered, malformed registry, version ≠ 1, covered-scope escape, README absent, corpus dir missing, non-corpus rows ignored). Live at round-57 base `7178bfd3`: the r56 verifier spotcheck file was `uncovered` — recomputed by `comm` over `find corpus/… -name '*.md'` vs README rows, 133 files / 132 rows; the row is added this round and the gate reads `CLEAN files=135 rows=135 covered=135`.
887:   - **Limit.** The gate binds the mapping, not the row's content: a row that exists but mis-describes its file is still CLEAN — description truth stays a reviewer/spot-check concern, same boundary the census keeps between well-formedness and taste.
888: 
889: - **Q49 — an admitted source's pinned capture is re-fetchable from outside the fleet's own verifier, and the re-fetch is recorded.** Grounding: `considerthese/2026-10-24.md` §Self-improvement ideas item 4 (independent source re-fetch — "a check outside the fleet's own verifier"), taken as the round's one considerthese proposal and grounded by demonstration, not by the reflection's say-so.
890:   - **Who checks.** The lane at round close (or the non-author spot-check): re-fetch one admitted source's URL live, sha256 the fresh bytes, and compare with the `.ufo/pins/source-captures.json` capture sha for that row; the located Gate quote is re-searched in the fresh bytes' tag-stripped normalized text. A source-capture gate CLEAN plus a byte-identical independent re-fetch is a two-observer claim; a drifted page is recorded as drift, never silently re-pinned in the same act.
891:   - **Command.** `curl -fsSL <url> -o /tmp/refetch.html && sha256sum /tmp/refetch.html` vs the row's capture sha; normalized quote search over the fresh bytes (python3 tag-strip). Round-58 demonstration (S122, 2026-10-24): fresh sha256 `ed0068fabe16e861a4be746dbd91db68c7fdef5742f08f6a51d3d26d209e9d41`, byte-identical to the pinned capture, 268296 bytes both, quote re-found.
892:   - **Fails when.** The URL no longer resolves; the fresh bytes' sha diverges from the pinned capture without the divergence being recorded; the located quote is absent from the fresh bytes' normalized text. A paywalled or vanished page fails the re-fetch arm honestly — the capture pin stands as the historical record and the drift is named.
893:   - **Shown able to fail.** The round-58 demonstration could have failed on all three arms (fetch, sha, quote); its passing output is recorded in `corpus/lessons/round-58.md` §considerthese. A synthetic divergence case is trivially constructible (flip one byte of the capture) and is the spot-check's cheapest re-derivation.
894:   - **Limit.** One source per round, sampled — this is a discernment tripwire, not a census; it binds nothing mechanically and does not replace `source-capture` (which binds committed bytes, not live truth).
895: 
896: - **Q50 — a tier or row count quoted in a lesson is the histogram re-derived from `corpus/SOURCES.md`, not a figure copied from a report.** Grounding: `considerthese/2026-10-24.md` item 1 (recount every number quoted), taken this round; the defect it would have caught is R58-V4 (the round-58 report said tier counts 96→99 A; the census histogram at that tip was A=102 B=13 C=8).
897:   - **Who checks.** The frozen counter `repair59-probe.mjs` arm B7: the lesson line `TIER59: A=<n> B=<n> C=<n> rows=<n>` must equal the probe's own count of registry rows at the measured rev.
898:   - **Command.** The probe, or the same split: a `| S### |` row's fourth cell is the tier. Round-59 after-state is `TIER59: A=104 B=14 C=8 rows=126`.
899:   - **Fails when.** The lesson line is absent, or any of the four integers disagrees with the registry at that rev. A hand-copied "96→99" fails.
900:   - **Shown able to fail.** At base `0f66ecd4` the lesson is absent, so B7 misses (`want TIER59: A=102 B=13 C=8 rows=123`). A one-integer lie in the line misses the same way.
901:   - **Limit.** It binds the one TIER59 line, not every number in the report. The report still has to quote the command.
902: 
903: - **Q51 — every lane commit between a round's base and its tip is named in that round's report's *Landed changes*, or an errata names it.** Grounding: `considerthese/2026-10-24.md` §Self-improvement ideas item 5 (post-report commit check — "diff the report's 'Landed changes' list against the commits between the round's base and the next spot-check, and list any unnamed commit"), taken as the round's one considerthese proposal and grounded by opening the instances it names (r49: `01b70bb`, `9237a72`, `c432cc9`; r55: `e7a0711`, `26c886d`, R55-V1 — bookkeeping commits the reports did not name), not by the reflection's say-so.
904:   - **Who checks.** The lane at round close: `git -C <lane> log --format=%H <base>..<tip>` against the hashes quoted in the fleet report's *Landed changes* section; the non-author spot-check repeats the comparison against the next spot-check's base.
905:   - **Command.** `git -C <lane> log --format=%H <base>..<tip>` and a grep of the report for each hash; a commit in the range with no name in the report is a defect.
906:   - **Fails when.** The range holds a commit the report does not name, and no errata names it either. The instances are real: the r49 and r55 reports each omitted bookkeeping commits the reflector had to list by hand.
907:   - **Shown able to fail.** Round-60's own range is the demonstration: the lane's report must name the freeze commit, the work commit, the wave-evidence commit and the close-receipt commit, and the count is re-derived from the range rather than asserted.
908:   - **Limit.** It binds the *naming* of commits, not their content, and it reads the report as filed bytes — a correction lands as an erratum appended after the filed bytes, never as a rewrite of them.
909: 
910: - **Q52 — every citation in a committed report, scorecard section or lesson names a real object (commit hash, file, line); a template token such as `__TIP__`, `__MEASURED__` or `__COMMITS__` is rejected.** Grounding: `corpus/lessons/round-60-verifier-spotcheck.md:171-174` (routed defect R60-V2) and its §1 row at `:26` — the filed round-60 report (`.ufo/reports/round-60/kumitate.md` at fleet commit `7b0581ed`) cites the lane tip, the measured revision and the third landed change by placeholder at lines 4, 5, 73, 88, 96 and 190, so none of those claims names an object a non-author can open.
911:   - **Who checks.** The lane before filing (report, the round's `SCORECARD.md` section, `corpus/lessons/round-<N>.md`); the non-author spot-check repeats it on the filed bytes. Verifier spot-check files are out of scope: they quote the tokens as the defect's subject, not as a citation.
912:   - **Command.** `grep -nE '__[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]*__' <file>` → empty; then every hex token cited as a commit resolves: `grep -oE '\b[0-9a-f]{7,40}\b' <file> | sort -u | while read h; do git -C <lane> cat-file -e "$h^{commit}" || echo "MISS $h"; done` → every `MISS` is a content digest found in `.ufo/pins/*.json`, never an unresolved commit; every cited path exists at the cited revision (`git cat-file -e <rev>:<path>`).
913:   - **Fails when.** Any template token survives into committed bytes; a hex token cited as a commit does not resolve and is not a pinned digest; a cited path is absent at the cited revision.
914:   - **Shown able to fail.** The round-60 report gives 6 placeholder hits (`grep -cE '__[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]*__'`). It still fails at lane HEAD `be4a820c`: the committed `SCORECARD.md` round-60 section keeps `__MEASURED__` at lines 2833 and 2847. Its hash half passes: 6 commit tokens resolve, and the one miss, `c7f7c401`, is the S126 capture's sha256 prefix, pinned twice in `.ufo/pins/source-captures.json`.
915:   - **Limit.** It binds the existence of a cited object, not whether that object supports the claim; that half belongs to Q53 and Q55. Filed bytes are never rewritten; a defect found after filing is repaired by an appended erratum that names the real objects.
916: 
917: - **Q53 — a report's claimed score equals its committed receipt and the round's `SCORECARD.md` section, for the same revision.** Grounding: `corpus/lessons/round-60-verifier-spotcheck.md:175-177` (routed defect R60-V3) and §2 at `:77-78` — the round-60 report's line 85 says the work commit `a745a3b0` reads `held=9/10`, "the only miss is A10", while the committed receipt `.ufo/waves/round-60/close/dispatch60-work.txt` and `SCORECARD.md:2830` both read `held=8/10` with A7 and A10 missed.
918:   - **Who checks.** The lane before filing; the non-author spot-check re-derives all three numbers from committed bytes and never accepts the report's own number.
919:   - **Command.** For each revision the report scores: `grep -oE 'held=[0-9]+/[0-9]+'` over the report's line for that revision, over the first line of the receipt it cites (`git show <tip>:<receipt>`, whose `rev=` field must equal that revision), and over the SCORECARD section's sentence for that revision → three identical `N/M` pairs. A miss list the report quotes ("the only miss is A10") must equal the receipt's `MISS` arms.
920:   - **Fails when.** Any of the three numbers differs, the receipt's `rev=` names another revision, the cited receipt is uncommitted, or the report's miss list omits a `MISS` arm in the receipt.
921:   - **Shown able to fail.** Round 60 at `165b8304` (the commit that landed the work receipt): report `held=9/10` (line 85) ≠ receipt `held=8/10 … rev=a745a3b0… | A7 MISS row-absent | A10 MISS exit=2` = `SCORECARD.md:2830` `held=8/10`; the report's miss list (A10 only) omits A7.
922:   - **Limit.** It binds agreement across the three artifacts, not the truth of the receipt; a receipt is evidence only when it was produced by the frozen command (Q43/Q44). When the receipt and the report disagree, the receipt wins and the report is corrected by an erratum.
923: 
924: - **Q54 — a claim that a wave was dispatched cites a committed dispatch record in the `dispatch-evidence` gate's schema, and every dead seat is named in the report with its last error text.** Grounding: `corpus/lessons/round-60-verifier-spotcheck.md:181-185` (routed defect R60-V5) and `:186-191` (R60-V6), with §2 at `:59-75`. Round 60 has no `dispatch-actual.json`. The launcher wrote `w1/swarm-registry.json`, whose `members` is an object with `agentId: null` on all 32 seats; the gate reads that as `REGISTRY_UNREADABLE:members-absent`, and its `NOT_A_DISPATCH` arm also applies. 27 of 32 seats settled `exit=-9 session=null`, and `w1-launcher.log` ends in a `ValueError` traceback, yet the report names no dead seat and says "the parent stayed alive until settlement" (line 10).
925:   - **Who checks.** The lane at round close; the non-author spot-check re-derives the dead set from `launcher-progress.tsv` at the committed tip.
926:   - **Command.** Schema half: `node scripts/dispatch-evidence.mjs --root <lane> --round <N> --wave <w>` → exit 0 `CLEAN` over committed bytes, which needs `.ufo/waves/round-<N>/<w>/dispatch-actual.json` with `members` as an array and a non-null `agentId` per dispatched seat. Without running the gate, use `jq -e '(.members|type=="array") and all(.members[]; .agentId != null)' dispatch-actual.json`. Dead-seat half: `awk -F'\t' '$4 != "exit=0" {print $1}' launcher-progress.tsv` gives the dead set, and each name must appear in the report as dead next to the text of its row's `err=` field. A launcher crash (`Traceback` in the launcher log) must be stated in the report.
927:   - **Fails when.** The dispatch record is absent, uncommitted or in another schema; any seat with `exit≠0` or `session=null` is missing from the report's dead list or has no error text; the report credits a dead seat; a launcher traceback goes unstated.
928:   - **Shown able to fail.** Round 60 at `165b8304`: `dispatch-actual.json` absent; `jq '.members|type' w1/swarm-registry.json` → `object`, non-null `agentId` count `0`; `awk` → `exit0=5 dead=27`. Of the 27 dead names, only `ConnectorSiblings` appears in the report at all, as a path to its seat report (line 198), not as dead; `w1-launcher.log:68` reads `ValueError: dictionary update sequence element #6 has length 1; 2 is required`.
929:   - **Limit.** The gate binds the record's shape and its agreement with the progress file. Whether the reported error text is the seat's real cause is still a reader's check against `<seat>.err` and the stream. A seat recorded dead after it committed useful bytes is still dead for crediting; its bytes count only where a live seat or the L1 re-derives them.
930: 
931: - **Q55 — a tip/after receipt cited by a report exists as a committed file at the measured revision's tip and carries the real observed line the report quotes.** Grounding: `corpus/lessons/round-60-verifier-spotcheck.md:178-180` (routed defect R60-V4) and §2 at `:67-69`. The round-60 report cites `close/dispatch60-tip.txt` and `close/doctrine60-tip.txt` (lines 89, 97) as the after-receipts for `DISPATCH60_HELD held=10/10` and `DOCTRINE60_HELD held=6/6`. Neither file existed anywhere in the repo at filing.
932:   - **Who checks.** The lane before filing; the non-author spot-check opens the receipt at the committed tip and never re-runs the counter to fill a gap.
933:   - **Command.** `git -C <lane> cat-file -e <tip>:<receipt>` → exit 0. The receipt's first line has `rev=<measured>`, where `<measured>` is the full hash the report names as its measured revision (not a placeholder, per Q52). The report's quoted after-line is a fixed-string substring of the receipt: `git show <tip>:<receipt> | grep -cF '<quoted line>'` → ≥ 1.
934:   - **Fails when.** The cited receipt is absent or uncommitted at the tip; its `rev=` differs from the report's measured revision; the report's quoted verdict, held count or exit code is not in the receipt's bytes.
935:   - **Shown able to fail.** At round-60 filing (`a745a3b0`, report `7b0581ed`) both cited receipts were absent (`find . -name '*tip.txt'` matched only rounds 36/41/51/57/58/59). Round 61 committed them in `be4a820c`, so the existence arm now passes. The content arm still fails for dispatch: `close/dispatch60-tip.txt` reads `DISPATCH60_UNMET held=8/10 … rev=a745a3b0…`, and `grep -cF 'DISPATCH60_HELD held=10/10'` → `0`, against the report's line 88. `close/doctrine60-tip.txt` carries `DOCTRINE60_HELD held=6/6 … rev=a745a3b0…`, which agrees with the report's held count. Its `rev=` match still cannot be checked, because the report's measured revision is `__MEASURED__`.
936:   - **Limit.** It binds the receipt to the report's quoted line and revision, not to a fresh run: the receipt must come from the frozen command (Q43/Q44) and be L1-bound (Q37). A receipt committed after filing repairs the citation only through an erratum that quotes the receipt's actual line, even when that line is worse than the claim.
937: 
938: - **Q56 — quarantine rows are bound to registry entries by document identity, never by numeric id.** Grounding: `corpus/lessons/round-61.md` §Mistakes (round 60 compared campaign ids from a separate namespace to lane ids and called rows "lane's own" without document matching).
939:   - **Who checks.** The lane before any quarantine disposition; a non-author spot-check re-opens the cited URL/DOI and compares it with the lane's source row.
940:   - **Command.** For each quarantine row, resolve its cited URL/DOI against `corpus/SOURCES.md` source cells and write `register-id → lane-id` or `no lane row` in the lesson; compare by normalized URL/DOI, not S-id equality.
941:   - **Fails when.** An id match is treated as document identity, or a shared document is missed because the two registries assigned different ids.
942:   - **Shown able to fail.** The round-60 lesson's S109/S116/S118 claim is false by document identity; round 61 maps register S109→lane S125, S118→lane S134 and S178→lane S194, while the ids themselves differ.
943:   - **Limit.** URL/DOI identity may miss source revisions or distinct claims on the same canonical URL; the lesson must still state scope and anchor.
944: 
945: - **Q57 — a frozen counter must reject a do-nothing control that skips the claimed activity, and must distinguish its honest-input control from an adversarial one.** Grounding: `corpus/lessons/round-61.md` §Mistakes (C1's fabricated zero-seat record reads HELD; C2's honest row misses while a forged record reads HELD).
946:   - **Who checks.** Before any seat scores, the lane freezes one positive control and one do-nothing/adversarial control; the non-author reviewer re-runs both against the same counter.
947:   - **Command.** Run the exact frozen counting command on the honest fixture and on the do-nothing fixture; record full verdict lines and exits in separate committed receipts.
948:   - **Fails when.** The do-nothing fixture reaches the declared HELD target, or the honest fixture cannot reach it under the frozen schema.
949:   - **Shown able to fail.** Round 61's `CritControlC1.md` reads `DISPATCH61_HELD held=4/4` for the zero-seat fabrication; `CritControlC2.md` reads 4/6 for honest work and 6/6 for a forged capture.
950:   - **Limit.** The controls test the declared predicate and its data path; they do not prove the external runtime's behavior unless the counter binds an independently emitted dispatch record.
951: 
952: - **Q58 — a round's `plan.md` is committed before that round's first wave marker, and the command that
953:   says so exits 0 for a closed round.** Grounding: `corpus/lessons/round-62-verifier-spotcheck.md`
954:   §Verdict (routed defect 1) — round 62 read "no 1–3 frozen claim sentences or counting predicates" in its prompt as "no
955:   claims declared" (`round-62-verifier-spotcheck.md:15`; routed defect 1 at `:57`) and filed a zero-claim round; it committed no `.ufo/waves/round-62/plan.md` at all,
956:   while `.ufo/waves/round-62/w2-dispatch.json` is committed at
957:   `6d8faede281e509a2201de504ffcb0f7781256fe`. Nothing in the lane could fail on that until this command
958:   existed. Measured at lane tip `b38a2065ab8ac5b198f6569b9013d04411c3d40d` (2026-10-25):
959:   `--round 62` → exit 1 `reason=NO_PLAN`.
960:   - **Who checks.** The lane L1 before it commits a wave's `.ready`, and again at close; the non-author
961:     closure re-runs the command at the round's tip revision and pastes the full verdict line.
962:   - **Field.** `.ufo/waves/round-<N>/plan.md` committed; the oldest commit that adds it is an
963:     ancestor-or-equal of the oldest commit that adds a top-level `.ufo/waves/round-<N>/*.ready`
964:     (fallback, only when no `.ready` was ever added: a top-level `*-dispatch.json`), and its committer
965:     time is `<=` that marker's. Pathspecs are glob-restricted (`:(glob)`) so a nested fixture marker
966:     under `controls/` can never stand in for the round's marker.
967:   - **Command.** `bash scripts/plan-before-ready.sh --round <N> --rev <tip> --earliest-marker` (the strictest reading: the earlier of the first `.ready` and the first `*-dispatch.json`; without the flag a `*-dispatch.json` committed before the plan passes whenever a later `.ready` exists) → one line
968:     `PLAN_BEFORE_READY: PASS rev=<tip> round=<N> ... plan=<sha> marker=<sha>` and exit 0. Self-test of the
969:     command itself: `bash scripts/plan-before-ready.sh --selftest` →
970:     `PLAN_BEFORE_READY_SELFTEST: PASS (10/10)` exit 0. Standing sweep: `bash scripts/plan-before-ready.sh --all`.
971:   - **Fails when.** Exit 1: `NO_PLAN` (a marker is committed and the plan never was — round 62),
972:     `PLAN_NOT_ANCESTOR` (the marker commit precedes the plan commit — the wrong-order fixture), or
973:     `PLAN_CT_AFTER_MARKER`. Exit 2 is **not** a pass for a closed round: `NO_MARKER` means the round
974:     committed no wave marker at all, so the ordering was never demonstrated (round 63 at `b38a206`
975:     reads `NA reason=NO_MARKER` until wave 1's `.ready` is committed).
976:   - **Shown able to fail.** `--round 62 --rev dfa6fca8` → exit 1, `reason=NO_PLAN`, marker
977:     `6d8faede281e509a2201de504ffcb0f7781256fe`; the selftest case `wrong-order-ready-first` (a fixture repo the script builds itself; its commits are throwaway and not citable) → exit 1 `reason=PLAN_NOT_ANCESTOR`; `--all` at `b38a206` → exit 1 with
978:     `failed=35,36,37,38,39,40,62`.
979:   - **Epoch.** The first round with a committed `plan.md` is round 41 (`34fccc170c73264faf5c27aaf7650d3419765ae0`);
980:     rounds 35-40 predate the convention and `--all` reports them `NO_PLAN` by design. The criterion
981:     applies from round 41 onward; a pre-41 round is not re-judged. The same `--all` run reads `NA` for rounds
982:     49 and 52-60 (`NO_MARKER`: their waves ran but committed no top-level marker) — their ordering is never judged;
983:     there is no check that turns "closed round with reports and no marker" into FAIL.
984:   - **Limit.** A plan and a marker committed together (round 50: `5b0de268e5a6bdd744fe47c6ee2ee58404693ac3`
985:     adds both `plan.md` and `r50-dispatch.json`) reads PASS, which cannot distinguish a pre-dispatch
986:     freeze from a same-commit write after dispatch; pair it with the round's `base/` freeze receipt and
987:     with C1's `inline-dispatch-evidence` gate, which binds seats to records the lane does not author.
988:     Committer time is lane-controlled and is a secondary arm only — the ancestry test is the real one. A
989:     history rewrite that makes the plan an ancestor of the marker is invisible to ordering alone, so the
990:     closure must pin the tip hash it judged.
991: 
992: - **Q59 — a dispatch claim is backed by host records the lane does not author (per-seat session transcripts, the orchestrator dispatcher log, committed bytes only), and the dead-seat set read from the transcripts is named in the report.** Grounding: `corpus/lessons/round-60-verifier-spotcheck.md` R60-V5/V6 (`:181-191`) — round 60's registry read `NOT_A_DISPATCH`, 27/32 seats settled `exit=-9 session=null`, and the report named no dead seat — with `considerthese/2026-10-25.md` idea 3 (audit seat deaths).
993:   - **Who checks.** The lane at round close, after committing the wave's `<wave>.ready`, `<wave>.ready.dispatched`, `<wave>-dispatch.json`, `<wave>-results.json` and seat reports; the non-author spot-check re-runs the same gate against the same host records and re-derives the dead set from the transcripts, never from `results.json`.
994:   - **Command.** `node scripts/inline-dispatch-evidence.mjs --root <lane> --rev <tip> --round <N> --wave <w> --report /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/.ufo/reports/round-<N>/kumitate.md` → exit 0 `INLINE_DISPATCH: CLEAN (seats=… sessions=… done=… reports=… dead=…)`; when it also prints `DEAD <names>`, every name appears in the report beside its last error text.
995:   - **Fails when.** A seat's transcript is absent, foreign, ambiguous or shares a session id with another seat; a `spawned` or `done` log line is missing or its count disagrees; a seat report is absent, under 64 bytes or byte-identical to another's; a dead seat's name is absent from the `--report` file; the dispatch/ready/results/context disagree (`READY_MISMATCH`, `DISPATCH_MISMATCH`, `RESULTS_MISMATCH`, `PARENT_MISMATCH`, a `done` line twice); a transcript is corrupt (`SESSION_CORRUPT`) or fails a shape arm (`SESSION_HEADER`, `SESSION_TOOL_JOIN`, `SESSION_ROWGRAPH`, `SESSION_TIMELINE`, `SESSION_TEMPLATE`); the wave reads `NOT_A_DISPATCH` or fail-closed (`WAVE_ABSENT`, `REV_UNREADABLE`, `DISPATCH_UNREADABLE`, `RESULTS_UNREADABLE`, `SESSIONS_ROOT_ABSENT`, `LOG_UNREADABLE`). A dead seat's own missing report is not a finding (it is named, not credited). Relation to Q54: Q54 binds the launcher-era record; Q59 binds the inline-era host records and carries the dead-seat clause forward.
996:   - **Shown able to fail.** The 75 committed controls (`controls/inline/`, 14 at the freeze plus the wave-1 and wave-2 ratchet cases; see `.ufo/waves/round-63/controls/CHANGES-AFTER-FREEZE.md`) each exit as their `expect` names — `honest` → `CLEAN` exit 0, `forged-no-sessions` → `NOT_A_DISPATCH`, `cheap-40-seats` (a 40-seat forgery of five hand-written rows per seat) → `SESSION_TOOL_JOIN`, `session-id-dup` → `SESSION_ID_DUP`, `reports-28-bytes` → `REPORT_TINY`, `results-name-swap` → `RESULTS_MISMATCH`; the real-host sweep `controls/inline-real-hosts.txt` reads `CLEAN` on kengaku r35 build/falsify and mori r47 w2, `DRIFT` on older dispatcher generations.
997:   - **Limit.** The limit `plan.md` states: a lane that also writes faithful transcripts into the host session store and lines into the orchestrator's log defeats the gate; those two records live outside the repository and the non-author closure re-derives them. The `--report` arm is a substring test on a file read live from disk (not `git show REV:`), so a report that names a dead seat anywhere, even in a success roster, satisfies it; `finished()` counts a seat that yielded and has no `session_exit` row as finished (wave 1: 6 of 40 seats were still idle when the dispatcher settled the wave) and no committed control locks that choice. The committed controls do not exercise the `DEAD_UNNAMED` arm (they run without `--report`); that arm is shown only by the gate's `--selftest` (`dead-unnamed-in-report` → `DRIFT [DEAD_UNNAMED]`, `dead-named-in-report` → `CLEAN dead=1`).
998: 
999: - **Q60 — a round's plan is not frozen while `readme-map` is red at the commit that carries it.** Grounding: the
1000:   R56-V3 `reference-drift` class at round start, not after close — round 63's verifier spot-check file landed
1001:   without its `corpus/README.md` row (`corpus/lessons/round-63-verifier-spotcheck.md:87`, routed defect D1), so
1002:   round 64's own plan commit reads `README_MAP: DRIFT files=154 rows=153 covered=153 bad=2
1003:   first=uncovered:lessons/round-63-verifier-spotcheck.md` exit 1 (`.ufo/waves/round-64/base/readme-map-before.txt`);
1004:   `corpus/lessons/round-64.md` §Mistakes row 1 records the class (`reference-drift`, captured-by `readme-map`
1005:   after the fact) with this criterion as its fix. Q48 catches the missing row at close; nothing caught it at the
1006:   freeze until this arm existed.
1007:   - **Who checks.** The lane L1 before it commits the round's `plan.md`; the non-author closure re-runs the
1008:     command at the round's tip and pastes the full verdict line. It is Q58's command with one more arm, so it
1009:     runs at the same two moments.
1010:   - **Field.** `PLAN` = the oldest commit that adds `.ufo/waves/round-<N>/plan.md`
1011:     (`git log --diff-filter=A --format=%H -- ':(glob).ufo/waves/round-<N>/plan.md'`). The map is judged at `PLAN`,
1012:     over `git archive PLAN` extracted to a temp dir, never over the worktree and never over the tip: a later
1013:     repair cannot make a red freeze green, and a tip read cannot make a green freeze red.
1014:   - **Command.** `bash scripts/plan-before-ready.sh --round <N>` → `PLAN_BEFORE_READY: PASS rev=<tip> round=<N> …
1015:     plan=<sha> … map=CLEAN files=<n> rows=<n> covered=<n>` exit 0 (for `<N> >= PBR_MAP_FROM`, default 65; for `<N> < PBR_MAP_FROM`, `map=SKIP reason=MAP_PRE_EPOCH_ROUND` unless `PBR_MAP_FROM=0` is set). The map arm runs `node scripts/readme-map.mjs`
1016:     inside the archive of `plan=<sha>` and requires exit 0 plus `README_MAP: CLEAN`; a red map fails the round
1017:     **before** the marker/ordering arms, so a round still in flight (plan committed, no `.ready` yet: the freeze
1018:     moment) cannot read `NA` over a red map. Standing sweep: `--all` (and `PBR_MAP_FROM=0 bash scripts/plan-before-ready.sh --all` for the historical pre-epoch audit).
1019:   - **Fails when.** The archived gate reads DRIFT (`reason=MAP_DRIFT`, the line carries
1020:     `map=DRIFT map_exit=1 map_first=<arm>:<path>`), FAIL-CLOSED (`reason=MAP_FAIL_CLOSED`), prints exit 0 without a
1021:     `CLEAN` verdict (`reason=MAP_NO_VERDICT`), cannot run (`reason=MAP_UNRUNNABLE`), or the gate existed before
1022:     `PLAN` yet is missing at `PLAN` (`reason=MAP_ABSENT`). Exit 2 is never a pass for a frozen plan. Q58's own arms
1023:     (`NO_PLAN`, `PLAN_NOT_ANCESTOR`, `PLAN_CT_AFTER_MARKER`) still fail the same run.
1024:   - **Shown able to fail.** Measured at lane freeze `dd1a3e6f19dc82c54ef67864c9ba87e4eb7c24ef` with the arm's
1025:     draft (`build/K64ExecReadmeGuard/plan-before-ready.sh`, equivalent to `PBR_MAP_FROM=0`):
1026:     round 64 → `PLAN_BEFORE_READY: FAIL … round=64 … reason=MAP_DRIFT plan=dd1a3e6f… marker=- … map=DRIFT
1027:     map_exit=1 map_first=uncovered:lessons/round-63-verifier-spotcheck.md`, exit 1; round 63 → the same reason at
1028:     its own plan `b38a2065ab8ac5b198f6569b9013d04411c3d40d`, `map_first=uncovered:lessons/round-62-verifier-spotcheck.md`.
1029:     Under `PBR_MAP_FROM=0`, `--all` → `pass=10 fail=12 na=8 rounds=all(30) … failed=35,36,37,38,39,40,58,60,61,62,63,64 na_rounds=49,52,53,54,55,56,57,59 map_red=58,60,61,63,64`, of which five are
1030:     this arm: rounds 58, 60, 61, 63, 64 — four of the five on the *previous* round's spot-check file (58 is
1031:     `orphan-row:lessons/round-58.md`, its own lesson). The pass side is live history too, not only a fixture:
1032:     under `PBR_MAP_FROM=0`, round 57's plan `f0dc6d1160e66af65355bd353665adac22bbf4a9` reads `map=CLEAN files=135 rows=135 covered=135` and
1033:     round 59's plan `c54943320249b76a7fef97404a50f130336e511c` reads `map=CLEAN files=141 rows=141 covered=141`
1034:     (both `NA reason=NO_MARKER` for want of a wave marker, the map arm green). As landed at `2ed8a5f8`: `PBR_MAP_FROM=0 bash scripts/plan-before-ready.sh --round 64` → `FAIL … reason=MAP_DRIFT` exit 1, default `--round 64` → `PASS … map=SKIP reason=MAP_PRE_EPOCH_ROUND` exit 0, default `--all` → `pass=13 fail=7 na=10 rounds=all(30) … failed=35,36,37,38,39,40,62 na_rounds=49,52,53,54,55,56,57,58,59,60 map_red=` exit 1, selftest `PLAN_BEFORE_READY_SELFTEST: PASS (18/18)` exit 0 (`.ufo/waves/round-64/build/K64ExecReadmeGuard/receipts/10-selftest.txt`, `.ufo/waves/round-64/build/K64R2ReviewQuality/receipts/plan-before-ready-r64.txt`). Draft-arm receipts: `build/K64ScribeQuality/q60-readme-map-at-plan-commit.txt`, `q60-draft-arm-run.txt`, `q60-draft-arm-sweep.txt`.
1035:   - **Limit.** It binds the map, not the row's content (Q48's limit, unchanged): a row that exists but mis-describes
1036:     its file is CLEAN. `covered` is lane-authored, so a plan commit that deletes a file *and* its row and its pin
1037:     reads CLEAN — a drift tripwire, not a coverage proof. It judges the plan commit only; a corpus file that lands
1038:     later in the round without its row is still Q48's catch at close. **The arm's own `--selftest` fires it:** `PLAN_BEFORE_READY_SELFTEST: PASS (18/18)` (`MAP_FROM=0` inside `run_selftest`) includes a red-map fixture (`MAP_DRIFT`), a silent-zero counter (`MAP_NO_VERDICT`), a fail-closed counter (`MAP_FAIL_CLOSED`), a removed gate (`MAP_ABSENT`), a green fixture and a pre-epoch fixture (`map=SKIP reason=MAP_PRE_EPOCH`).
1039:   - **Epoch.** Enforced from round 65 (`PBR_MAP_FROM`, default 65, in `scripts/plan-before-ready.sh`). By default (`PBR_MAP_FROM=65`), rounds 35–40 read `map=SKIP reason=NO_PLAN` and every round 41–64 with a committed `plan.md` short-circuits before `map_at_plan` with `map=SKIP reason=MAP_PRE_EPOCH_ROUND`, so default `--all` keeps Q58's historical verdicts (`pass=13 fail=7 na=10`). Round 64 is the RED-BEFORE case: its
1040:     plan was frozen at `dd1a3e6f` over a red map before the arm existed, so `bash scripts/plan-before-ready.sh --round 64` reads
1041:     `map=SKIP reason=MAP_PRE_EPOCH_ROUND` PASS by default (once `w1.ready` is committed; `NA reason=NO_MARKER` at `dd1a3e6f`) and `PBR_MAP_FROM=0 bash scripts/plan-before-ready.sh --round 64` reads
1042:     `FAIL reason=MAP_DRIFT … map_first=uncovered:lessons/round-63-verifier-spotcheck.md` exit 1 (named, not hidden by the epoch). Under `PBR_MAP_FROM=0`, rounds 35–40 read
1043:     `map=SKIP reason=NO_PLAN` and rounds 41–56 `map=SKIP reason=MAP_PRE_EPOCH` (the gate post-dates their plans);
1044:     rounds 49, 52–57 and 59 read `NA` for want of a wave marker, so the map arm is judged on seven historical rounds —
1045:     57 and 59 CLEAN, 58, 60, 61, 63, 64 DRIFT. Those five keep their `MAP_DRIFT` verdict under `PBR_MAP_FROM=0` as historical evidence of
1046:     the recurrence, not as retroactive rejection under the default epoch.
1047:   - **Supersedes.** None. Q58's marker-ordering test, its selftest floor and its epoch are unchanged; Q48 stays the
1048:     close-time gate.
