1050: - **Q61 — a round's report is diffed against the committed receipts it cites before it is filed, and the diff reads CLEAN.** Grounding: round-60's report as filed (fleet commit `7b0581ed63a46ac1961b1ecf98ec0caf561ccd9b`, `.ufo/reports/round-60/kumitate.md`) carries six template tokens — `__TIP__` at line 4, `__MEASURED__` at 5, 88, 96, 190 and `__COMMITS__` at 73 — and line 88 reads `DISPATCH60_HELD held=10/10` while the lane's own committed receipt `.ufo/waves/round-60/close/dispatch60-tip.txt` reads `DISPATCH60: DISPATCH60_UNMET held=8/10 checks=10 rev=a745a3b0e02253e722834ef95042d97ed92e5e53 rule=A60` (R60-V2/V3/V4), with `considerthese/2026-10-25.md` idea 2 ("diff reports against receipts") and `corpus/lessons/round-64.md` §Mistakes row 2 (`unreceipted-tally`, `:13`) / §What round 64 changes (`:20`). Q52, Q53 and Q55 named those three defects one at a time and by hand; this is their mechanical counterpart, one command over the report's bytes.
1051:   - **Who checks.** The lane before it files the round's report, and again before it commits the round's close receipts (the diff reads receipts at the tip, so a receipt that lands after filing must be re-diffed); the non-author spot-check re-runs the same command on the filed bytes and never accepts the report's own numbers.
1052:   - **Command.** `node scripts/report-receipt-diff.mjs --lane <lane> --round <N> --report <file> --rev <lane tip>` → `REPORT_RECEIPT: CLEAN (round=<N> rev=<tip> bytes=<n>)` exit 0. DRIFT prints one line per finding and exits 1; exit 2 is fail-closed (unreadable report or rev); exit 64 is usage. Finding ids: `PLACEHOLDER`, `TALLY_UNRECEIPTED`, `TALLY_CHECKS_MISMATCH`, `RECEIPT_MISSING`, `RECEIPT_EMPTY`, `HASH_DEAD`, `HASH_ORPHAN`, `SECTION_MISSING`, `SHONEN_COUNT` (contract `kumitate-report-receipt-diff-v2`). `--fleet <dir>` adds the fleet repo to hash resolution.
1053:   - **Fails when.** Any of the nine findings fires: a template token (`PLACEHOLDER`: `__name__`, `{{NAME}}`, `LANE_HASH`, `TBD`, `XXXX`, `to be filled`, `<measured>`/`<measured_rev>`/`<tip_hash>`/`<rev_hash>`/`<placeholder>`/`<tbd>`/`<todo>`); a labelled `<LABEL>_HELD|UNMET held=x/y` that no committed receipt line (or none of the receipts cited on the claim's own line) carries with the same label *and* the same x/y (`TALLY_UNRECEIPTED`); a claim's `checks=k` that disagrees with the receipt carrying that pair (`TALLY_CHECKS_MISMATCH`); a `.ufo/waves/round-<N>/(base|close)/<file>` path the report names that is absent at the rev, escapes with `..`, is a symlink, or is an empty dir/unmatched glob (`RECEIPT_MISSING`); a cited receipt that exists at the rev but has no non-whitespace bytes (`RECEIPT_EMPTY`); a 39- or 40-hex hash (outside URL path components) that resolves in neither repo (`HASH_DEAD`), or a 40-hex hash that resolves in the lane but is not an ancestor of the rev (`HASH_ORPHAN`); one of the six required headings (`Work performed`, `Landed changes`, `Before → after measurements`, `Sources & frontier`, `Trend verdicts`, `SHONEN`) absent outside fenced blocks (`SECTION_MISSING`); the `SHONEN` heading not occurring exactly once in prose or carrying fewer than four box markers inside its section (`SHONEN_COUNT`). A cited receipt that is missing is a finding even when the report's number happens to be right.
1054:   - **Shown able to fail.** Run now at lane rev `dd1a3e6f`: the round-60 report as filed → `REPORT_RECEIPT: DRIFT PLACEHOLDER,TALLY_UNRECEIPTED (round=60 rev=dd1a3e6f… bytes=13611)` exit 1, with exactly six `PLACEHOLDER` lines and `TALLY_UNRECEIPTED DISPATCH60_HELD held=10/10` — matching an independent `grep -o '__[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]*__' | wc -l` of the same bytes (6); the round-63 report as filed (fleet `8fd46e614d6db3ca251b9ce75cdc7b94ecb574ad`) → `REPORT_RECEIPT: CLEAN (round=63 rev=dd1a3e6f… bytes=17479)` exit 0. The v2 tool's `--selftest` reads `REPORT_RECEIPT_SELFTEST: PASS (52/52)` exit 0 (v1 at freeze read `PASS (20/20)` in `build/K64ScribeQuality/q61-r63-report-clean.txt`), and `.ufo/waves/round-64/controls/receipt/` holds 37 committed cases (16 frozen `c0-honest` … `c15-honest-two-receipts` plus 20 forgeries `k1`…`k20` and `c16`, `controls/CHANGES-AFTER-FREEZE.md`), each exiting as its `expect` names across 8 distinct finding ids. Receipts: `build/K64ScribeQuality/q61-r60-report-drift.txt`, `q61-r63-report-clean.txt` (v1), `build/K64R2ReviewQuality/receipts/q61-v2-selftest-and-controls.txt` (v2).
1055:   - **Limit.** The tool's declared limits, restated and one of them measured: only labelled tallies are compared — a bare `held=9/10` cannot be told from a plan's target, so an unlabelled overstatement passes (probe now: a report whose body claims `held=9/10` twice, diffed against round 64's base receipt which reads `held=0/5`, returns `REPORT_RECEIPT: CLEAN (round=64 rev=dd1a3e6f… bytes=437)` exit 0 — `q61-cheap-lie-bare-tally.txt`), and a selftest tally like `PASS (69/69)` is likewise outside `<LABEL>_HELD|UNMET` (`corpus/lessons/round-64.md:13`); a receipt the lane itself wrote is trusted as written, so a report and a receipt that agree on a wrong number read CLEAN (Q43/Q44's frozen-command rule still binds the receipt); `HASH_DEAD` cannot resolve a hash of an external repository, so a foreign commit hash is a finding only when it is 39- or 40-hex (outside a URL) and absent from both repos; the `--report` bytes are read from disk, not from `git show REV:`, so the file must be diffed as filed. The `--rev` arm trusts the lane's own history: `HASH_ORPHAN` catches a commit on another branch, not a hash that is an ancestor of the tip but supports nothing the report says. The unlabelled-tally hole is the ratchet's first candidate: a control pinning that behaviour (a report with a bare `held=x/y` that disagrees with its receipt reads CLEAN) would make any future strengthening visible instead of silent.
1056:   - **Supersedes.** None. Q52 (tokens and resolvable citations), Q53 (report = receipt = SCORECARD section) and Q55 (a cited receipt exists and carries the quoted line) stay in force; Q61 makes their token, tally, receipt-path and hash arms mechanical and leaves Q53's third-copy comparison against `SCORECARD.md` and Q55's `rev=` agreement to their own rows.
1057: 
1058: - **Q51-C1 — correction to Q51's grounding (append-only; Q51's bytes are not rewritten).** Grounding: `corpus/lessons/round-63-verifier-spotcheck.md:91` (routed defect D5) and `corpus/lessons/round-64.md:114` (`## Open items carried`). Q51's grounding opens the r49 instances it names as `01b70bb`, `9237a72`, `c432cc9`. `9237a72` resolves in neither repository: `git -C /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kumitate-shokunin cat-file -t 9237a72` → `fatal: Not a valid object name 9237a72`, exit 128, and the same in `/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin`; no object in the lane's object database begins `9237`. The object Q51 meant is the round-49 record addendum `923a172` (a digit transposition), which the r49 spot-check file cites correctly at `corpus/lessons/round-49-verifier-spotcheck.md:10` — "`01b70bb0` (C2 addendum, C16 + prior art), `923a172` (record addendum, re-score 16/16), `c432cc9` (ConnSiblingOverlap seat report)" — and which resolves in the lane as `round-49: record addendum — C2 re-scored 16/16 at 01b70bb0, LOG line for prior-art citations and the mount-binds disambiguation`. Q51's other cited instances resolve (`01b70bb`, `c432cc9`, `e7a0711`, `26c886d`: `commit` in the lane, absent in the fleet, as expected for lane commits).
1059:   - **Who checks.** The lane before citing a commit in any QUALITY grounding; the non-author spot-check re-resolves the commit-shaped hex tokens of the row it is judging.
1060:   - **Command.** For each hex token the row presents as a commit: `git -C <lane> cat-file -e <h>^{commit} || git -C <fleet> cat-file -e <h>^{commit}` → exit 0. `9237a72` fails both.
1061:   - **Fails when.** A token presented as a commit resolves in neither repo, or resolves to a non-commit object. A token presented as a content digest, sha256 prefix or selftest seed is out of scope, exactly as Q52's pin carve-out states.
1062:   - **Shown able to fail.** The blanket sweep `grep -oE '\b[0-9a-f]{7,40}\b' corpus/QUALITY.md | sort -u` (55 unique tokens at `dd1a3e6f` before Q60–Q51-C1 were appended; 64 at `2ed8a5f8` after appending Q60–Q51-C1, all 9 newly added tokens resolving as commits in the lane or fleet) yields nine non-resolving tokens: `0011223344556677` and `aabbccddeeff0011` (selftest seeds, line 546), `03a258d6`, `0c1f9b22`, `3a32dd34`, `6faa34ab`, `d6068d1b` (content digests, lines 766, 845, 320, 745, 320), `c7f7c401` (pinned in `.ufo/pins/source-captures.json` and `source-dupes.json`) and `9237a72` — the only one presented as a commit and resolving nowhere. Receipt: `build/K64ScribeQuality/q51-hash-resolution.txt`.
1063:   - **Limit.** It corrects the pointer, not the rule: Q51 (every lane commit between a round's base and its tip is named in the report) is unchanged and its r49/r55 instances stand once `9237a72` is read as `923a172`. It also shows Q52's scope does not cover `corpus/QUALITY.md` (Q52 names "report, scorecard section or lesson"), which is why a broken grounding hash could sit in the admission bar — the L1 may extend Q52's scope rather than rely on this row.
1064:   - **Supersedes.** Q51's grounding pointer only; Q51's rule is untouched.
1065: 
1066: - **Q62 — a capability's registry home is three places or it is not home (round 68) — a `SKILL.md`
1067:   gate-registry row naming the script, a `corpus/QUALITY.md` criterion naming the capability, and a
1068:   `SCORECARD.md` `## Capabilities` row whose first cell names it — and all three name the same round.**
1069:   Grounding: `corpus/lessons/round-68.md` §Mistakes (`registry-home`, round 68). Measured at the round-68
1070:   freeze `39f61816d4ee7a8d401df42c1818c91a9c537bce`: `grep -c 'routed-ledger\.mjs' SKILL.md` → `0`,
1071:   `grep -c 'routed-ledger' corpus/QUALITY.md` → `0`, `grep -c '^| \`routed-ledger\`' SCORECARD.md` → `0`,
1072:   while `grep -c 'routed-ledger' SCORECARD.md` → `1` — `SCORECARD.md:3003`, the round-66 C1 line that itself
1073:   reads "No capability row is entered". The three arms are already the tool's own L6 predicates, and read
1074:   all-false at round 66: `LEDGER66_UNMET held=0/6 checks=6 rev=8d557f85312de4fcc82e09ff735d21436bc3746d
1075:   rule=L66 seed=0d44321a076abff3 | … | L6 MISS skill-row=false quality=false capability-row=false`
1076:   (`.ufo/waves/round-66/base/ledger66-base.txt`). The split-round precedent the third arm exists to catch:
1077:   `receipt-evidence` landed one round after its acquisition — `SCORECARD.md:1797` carries first-working round
1078:   `58` and the row text "Row added in round 59: the round-58 acquisition landed the gate and the pin, and the
1079:   capabilities table did not gain the row (R58-V6)".
1080:   - **Who checks.** The lane L1 in the integration change that lands the capability, before the round's
1081:     close; the non-author closure re-runs the three greps at the round's tip and compares the round token.
1082:   - **Field.** Three independent documents: `SKILL.md`'s gate table (`| name | kind | entry command | self-test |
1083:     pinned values live in |`, header at `SKILL.md:605`) — a data row whose first cell is the gate name and whose
1084:     entry command names the script; `corpus/QUALITY.md` — one criterion whose bold sentence names the capability
1085:     and carries its `(round N)`; `SCORECARD.md` `## Capabilities` (`SCORECARD.md:1777`) — a table row whose
1086:     **first cell** is the backticked capability name. Prose, a `## Round criteria` paragraph, a move-log line or
1087:     the inventory paragraph above the table is not a row.
1088:   - **Command.** For capability `<cap>` and round `<N>`:
1089:     `grep -c "<cap>\.mjs" SKILL.md` ≥ 1; `grep -c "<cap>" corpus/QUALITY.md` ≥ 1 with the matching row carrying
1090:     `(round <N>)`; `grep -c "^| \`<cap>\`" SCORECARD.md` ≥ 1 whose last cell reads `<N>`. The lane's own counter
1091:     for the capability must read `L6 … capability-row=true` at the judged revision. Receipt:
1092:     `build/K68ScribeQuality/registry-home-census.txt`.
1093:   - **Fails when.** Any of the three counts is 0; a capability is named only in SCORECARD prose, a QUALITY
1094:     narrative, a LOG bullet or a report; a SKILL row names the file but not the entry command; or the three
1095:     documents carry different rounds (`First-working round 58` / row "added in round 59" / a SKILL parenthetical
1096:     naming another round) for one capability.
1097:   - **Shown able to fail.** The census command above at the round-68 freeze prints `0 / 0 / 0` against a
1098:     capability that `SCORECARD.md:3003` already discusses by name (`SCORECARD_prose_mentions=1`) — the prose arm
1099:     is not the row arm. Round 66's counter reads the same three arms false on the same capability
1100:     (`.ufo/waves/round-66/base/ledger66-base.txt`). The row-late precedent is `SCORECARD.md:1797`
1101:     (`receipt-evidence`) and `cite-sources` (`SKILL checklist item 29`, first-working round 59).
1102:   - **Limit.** It binds the existence and the round token of three rows, not their agreement in content: a SKILL
1103:     row can carry a stale entry command, a QUALITY criterion can state a weaker rule than the tool implements, and
1104:     a SCORECARD row can overstate what the capability does — all three still pass. It also cannot tell a row
1105:     landed before the round's `.ready` from one written at close (Q58's limit): the three-row check is a
1106:     presence-and-round test, and the round column is lane-authored.
1107:   - **Supersedes.** None. Q53 (report = receipt = SCORECARD section) and Q48/Q60 (corpus rows and map coverage)
1108:     stay in force; this row is the capability-scoped, three-document form of the same bar.
1109: 
1110: - **Q63 — a receipt names the revision it measured: every probe receipt carries `rev=<full 40-hex sha>` on its
1111:   verdict line, and a receipt that quotes a tip without that tip's committed receipt is a routed defect
1112:   (round 68).** Grounding: `corpus/lessons/round-68.md` §Mistakes (`unreceipted-tip`, round 68), from the r67
1113:   routed D2 lineage (`corpus/lessons/round-67-verifier-spotcheck.md:71`). The r67 freeze commit
1114:   `993a7b16` carries `.ufo/waves/round-67/plan.md` and `.ufo/waves/round-67/probe/ledger67-probe.mjs` and
1115:   nothing else; its `base/` and `controls/` are empty, git cannot commit an empty directory, and yet the plan's
1116:   Before lines name six base receipts and two base tallies — `plan.md:77` (`LEDGER67_UNMET held=0/7` exit 1,
1117:   `base/ledger67-base.txt`), `:79`, `:81`, `:132` (`DEPREC67_UNMET held=0/10`, `base/deprec67-base.txt`), `:134`,
1118:   `:141` — all at base `f29eb699`, none committed. The positive side is this round's own freeze: both base
1119:   receipts carry the full sha (`ledger68-base.txt` and `deprec68-base.txt`, each `rev=d23892ad44b41e1af63b3edb949d265ca1dd812d`).
1120:   - **Who checks.** The lane before it commits a round's `base/` freeze receipts and again at close for `close/`;
1121:     the non-author closure re-derives each receipt's `rev=` and resolves the commit itself, never the report's copy.
1122:   - **Command.** For every receipt under `.ufo/waves/round-<N>/{base,close}/` that carries a verdict or a
1123:     `<LABEL>_HELD|_UNMET ... held=x/y` tally: the line matches `rev=[0-9a-f]{40}\b`, and
1124:     `git -C <lane> cat-file -e <rev>^{commit}` exits 0; a report or plan sentence of the form "at tip/cutoff/base
1125:     `<sha>`" must be backed by a receipt in the same round's `base/` or `close/` naming that sha. Receipts:
1126:     `build/K68ScribeQuality/freeze-receipts-r67-vs-r68.txt`.
1127:   - **Fails when.** A verdict/tally receipt carries no `rev=`; `rev=` is abbreviated, a branch name, `HEAD`, a
1128:     date, a worktree path or a scratch path; the named revision does not resolve in the lane at close and the
1129:     receipt does not say why; or a quoted tip has no committed receipt of its own. A **fixture** receipt
1130:     (a do-nothing control, a mutant fixture, a self-built repo) may name a revision that is deliberately
1131:     throwaway, but then the line must say so and carry what makes the run reproducible: the fixture-creation
1132:     command and the sha256 of the tool bytes it ran. A bare unresolvable `rev=` with neither is
1133:     indistinguishable from a fabricated one.
1134:   - **Shown able to fail.** r67: `git ls-tree -r --name-only 993a7b16 .ufo/waves/round-67/` →
1135:     `plan.md`, `probe/ledger67-probe.mjs`; `ls -la .ufo/waves/round-67/base/` → an empty directory — so the six
1136:     receipts the plan names cannot exist at the freeze (receipt `build/K68ScribeQuality/freeze-receipts-r67-vs-r68.txt`).
1137:     This is round 60's `__MEASURED__`/`__TIP__` class (Q61) at the freeze edge rather than at filing. Round 68's own
1138:     controls, same arm: `controls/c1-donothing.txt` (`rev=3ec65c91b208142392690aec43c44657fbdc16ad`),
1139:     `controls/c1-autoledger.txt` (`rev=3ab64d18c37ce2db0851af755d6ebe3633f4dd6a`) and
1140:     `controls/c2-donothing.txt` (`rev=70434c290f7dd2f32ea868a75989f357d0ff0f3b`) each fail
1141:     `git cat-file -e <rev>^{commit}` in **both** the lane and the fleet repo, and none carries a `fixture` token or
1142:     a fixture-creation command — so the do-nothing controls cannot be re-verified from their receipts
1143:     (`grep '^control=' .ufo/waves/round-68/controls/c1-donothing.txt` prints `control=donothing exit=1 rev=3ec65c91…`).
1144:   - **Limit.** Scoped to receipts that carry a verdict or tally: 20 of the 43 base receipts under rounds 64–68
1145:     carry no `rev=` (`grep -L 'rev=' .ufo/waves/round-6[4-8]/base/*.txt | wc -l` → `20`) and are census, selftest
1146:     or preflight dumps, which this row does not judge — a scope boundary, not an exemption to widen silently. A
1147:     `rev=` binds bytes to a revision, not to a clock, a machine or an author (Q39, Q44): a receipt written after
1148:     the fact can name the right sha and still be fabricated, so `receipt-attest`'s nonce arm and Q61's
1149:     `HASH_DEAD`/`TALLY_UNRECEIPTED` stay in force. A scratch or `/tmp` argv echoed into a receipt is not citable
1150:     evidence, whatever its `rev=`.
1151:   - **Supersedes.** None. It adds the missing arm of Q55 (a cited receipt exists and carries the quoted line):
1152:     Q55 never required the receipt to name the revision it measured.
