1154: - **Q64 — a frozen counter carries its exercised base receipt in the same freeze commit: a counter whose first
1155:   run happens after dispatch is unexercised and cannot freeze (round 68).** Grounding:
1156:   `corpus/lessons/round-68.md` §Mistakes (`unexercised-counter`, round 68) — the r67 draft counter
1157:   `.ufo/waves/round-67/probe/ledger67-probe.mjs` was committed at `993a7b16` without ever having run: its preamble
1158:   creates `${TMPDIR}/archive` (`ledger67-probe.mjs:71`), `extract()` calls `mkdirSync(dst)` on that same path
1159:   (`:79`), and the call at `:92` therefore throws before any check — no verdict line, exit 1. The plan the wrap-up
1160:   committed alongside it declares the receipts that never existed (`plan.md:77`, `:132`).
1161:   - **Who checks.** The lane L1 at the freeze, **before** it commits the round's `.ready`; the non-author closure
1162:     re-runs each base receipt's argv inside the archive of the freeze commit and compares the final line.
1163:   - **Command.** For each counter the plan names:
1164:     `git ls-tree -r --name-only <freeze> .ufo/waves/round-<N>/base/` lists a receipt whose line carries that
1165:     counter's own label and `<UNMET|HELD> held=<x>/<y> checks=<y> rev=<base>` plus its exit; then re-run the
1166:     receipt's argv verbatim against the archived tree and require the identical final line. Round-68 positive:
1167:     `git ls-tree -r --name-only 39f61816 .ufo/waves/round-68/base/` →
1168:     `census-before.txt`, `deprec68-base.txt`, `ledger68-base.txt`, the last two reading
1169:     `… rev=d23892ad44b41e1af63b3edb949d265ca1dd812d rule=L68` / `… rule=M68`.
1170:   - **Fails when.** A counter named in the plan has no base receipt in the freeze commit; a receipt exists but
1171:     carries no verdict line (crash, usage exit 64, or FAIL-CLOSED on its own base); its `rev=` is not the base the
1172:     plan declares; or the re-run's final line differs from the receipt's.
1173:   - **Shown able to fail.** `node build/K68ScribeQuality/ledger67-probe-as-frozen.mjs <lane>
1174:     d23892ad44b41e1af63b3edb949d265ca1dd812d --seed 2583a841b9d97d5e` → `Error: EEXIST: file already exists,
1175:     mkdir '…/archive' at extract (…ledger67-probe-as-frozen.mjs:79:3)`, exit 1, no verdict line
1176:     (`build/K68ScribeQuality/r67-unexercised-counter-crash.txt`; the exercised copy's blob hash `3a3a45a99daf…`
1177:     equals `993a7b16:.ufo/waves/round-67/probe/ledger67-probe.mjs`, so it is the frozen draft, not a rewrite).
1178:     r67's freeze tree carries no receipt at all (`build/K68ScribeQuality/freeze-receipts-r67-vs-r68.txt`).
1179:   - **Limit.** It judges exercise, not adequacy: a counter that runs and returns UNMET on its base proves the code
1180:     path executes and fails honestly there — it does not prove its checks are satisfiable at all (C1's L1..L7 and
1181:     C2's M1..M10 with their controls, Q57). A receipt committed in the same commit as the plan still does not
1182:     prove the run preceded dispatch (Q58's limit); the arm removes the "never ran" class only. `--seed`-carrying
1183:     counters must repeat the seed or the mutant set differs; a counter whose base arm is vacuous by design (C2's
1184:     M5 at base) must say so in its own receipt.
1185:   - **Supersedes.** None. Q57 (do-nothing control re-run by a non-author) and Q58 (plan committed before the first
1186:     marker) stay in force; this row is the third freeze-time fact: the counter itself has run.
