1199: 
1200: - **Q66 — live-arm receipts declare live state (round 69).** Grounding: `corpus/lessons/round-69.md` Mistakes, round-68 routed item 4. A receipt records `live=exercised` or `live=no-live(vacuous-declared)`. Red: round-68/base/deprec68-base.txt has no live field; green: round-69/base/deprec69-base.txt does. A no-live receipt never proves an origin claim.
1201: - **Q67 — settled outputs and report files are counted separately (round 69).** Grounding: `corpus/lessons/round-69.md`, round-68 routed item 3. At WAVE-DONE compare every result name with its nonempty regular report file and name exceptions in the receipt. Red: K68ReviewC1Predicate has a result but no w1 report. Never infer report existence from settlement.
1202: - **Q68 — registration triad is explicit (round 69).** Grounding: `corpus/lessons/round-69.md` and `considerthese/2026-10-26.md` idea 3, mined 2026-10-30. A newly acquired gate needs a SKILL registry row, its tool pin, and a demonstrated SCORECARD capability row. Red: round-65 harm-matrix lacks the registry/capability rows at its tip; do not call that conformant. Existing debt stays named, not silently reclassified.
1203: - **Q69 — the round-total seat count is checked against the campaign band, not a single wave's validator band (round 70).** Grounding: `corpus/lessons/round-70.md` and `considerthese/2026-10-26.md` proposal 4, opened 2026-10-30. Sum distinct dispatched seats across the round, including residual calls; record role mix and attack share separately. A v1 wave validated at 45 does not meet a round floor of 64. Red exemplar: `.ufo/waves/round-65/w1-dispatch.json` counts.total=45 while campaign minimum=64. Record the current round's observed WAVE-DONE/results census before claiming conformance; prepared payloads are not dispatch proof. Routing share is recorded from actual host configuration, never inferred from a stale alias label.
1204: - **Q70 — every N/N tally in SCORECARD, SKILL, or a report must name a committed transcript path or be marked unverifiable (round 74).** Grounding: `considerthese/2026-10-26.md` proposal 1 ("Check that every number has a transcript"), mined 2026-11-04 in round 74; defects R63-D2 (selftest tallies stated in prose without a transcript, 69/69) and R64-D1 (125 cases stated in prose versus a committed 52/52).
1205:   - **Who checks.** The lane before filing a report or committing SCORECARD/SKILL updates; the non-author closure re-verifies each cited tally against its committed transcript file.
1206:   - **Command.** For each `N/N` tally or integer count claim in `SCORECARD.md`, `SKILL.md`, or a filed round report: `grep -oE '[0-9]+/[0-9]+' <file>` and verify that the sentence cites a committed transcript or receipt path under `.ufo/waves/round-<N>/` containing that exact tally (`git show <rev>:<path> | grep -F '<tally>'`); any tally without a resolvable committed transcript must carry an explicit `unverifiable` or `recalled` label (Q3 discipline).
1207:   - **Fails when.** An `N/N` case count, selftest tally, or checklist score appears in prose without citing a committed transcript path; the cited transcript path does not exist at the judged commit; the transcript's recorded tally differs from the prose claim; or an unreceipted number is claimed without being marked unverifiable.
1208:   - **Shown able to fail.** `considerthese/2026-10-26.md` §Things worth watching item 2: round 63 claimed 69/69 in prose without a transcript, and round 64 cited 125 cases against a committed 52/52.
1209:   - **Limit.** Scoped to `N/N` tallies and case counts in `SCORECARD.md`, `SKILL.md`, and round reports; historical round sections are not rewritten in place (append-only); does not replace gate-level diffing (`report-receipt-diff`).
1210:   - **Supersedes.** None. Deepens Q3 (dated re-run or recalled label for counts) and Q24/Q55 (receipt-integrity disciplines) by requiring explicit transcript paths for fractional and ratio tallies.
1211: 
1212: - **Q71 — a round lesson's `## Gate` source ids must exist in the landed registry and agree with its `used-by` column (round 75).** Grounding: `considerthese/2026-10-26.md` proposal 2 ("Cross-check gate tables against the registry"), mined 2026-11-04 in round 75; defect class: round-65 D1 mapped S204–S206 in the Gate table differently from the landed SOURCES rows and claimed an S206 that was not added.
1213:   - **Who checks.** The lane before committing a lesson that adds or cites source rows; the non-author closure re-runs the same commands on the committed bytes.
1214:   - **Command.** `for id in $(grep -oE 'S[0-9]{3,}' corpus/lessons/round-<N>.md | sort -u); do grep -qE "^\|[[:space:]]*$id[[:space:]]*\|" corpus/SOURCES.md || echo "MISSING $id"; done` plus, for every id the Gate says grounds `corpus/knowledge/<entry>.md`, `grep -F "$id" <entry> >/dev/null || echo "NOT-USED $id <entry>"`; and the reverse check `grep -E "^\|[[:space:]]*S[0-9]+" corpus/SOURCES.md` rows whose `used-by` names the new lesson must be cited in that lesson.
1215:   - **Fails when.** A Gate row cites an id that the registry does not carry; a Gate row says an id grounds an entry whose provenance line does not name it; or a mined row's `used-by` names the new lesson while the Gate omits it.
1216:   - **Shown able to fail.** The r65 D1 rows (S204–S206) against the landed registry: the id set in the Gate differs from the registry's (the defect the criterion encodes).
1217:   - **Limit.** Judges id existence and pointer agreement, not whether the quote grounds the claim (that is the closure's spot-check); append-only rows mean a superseded id stays resolvable by design.
1218:   - **Supersedes.** None. Adds the registry half Q65/Q70 leave to receipts.
1219: 
1220: 
1221: - **Q72 — every round lesson carries a `## Counters` table, and a counter that rose without a mention is a defect (round 77).** Grounding: `considerthese/2026-10-26.md` proposal 6 ("Plot noisy counters across rounds"), mined 2026-11-04 in round 77; the observables are already computed every round (proxy findings, census entries/findings, README/spotcheck uncovered, SOURCES rows/tiers) but a rise is noticed only when a spot-check happens to look (r76's open proxy stanza was red while its report named only the map).
1222:   - **Who checks.** The lane L1 before the round lesson commits; the non-author closure re-derives one row of the table from its receipt.
1223:   - **Field.** `corpus/lessons/round-<N>.md` carries a `## Counters` table with columns `| counter | open | close | source |`; one row per named counter, each value accompanied by the command or the committed receipt path that produced it; any rise is named in the round report or `## Limits`. The table's rows are the round's own observables — no counter may enter without a command that reads it.
1224:   - **Command.** `sed -n '/^## Counters/,/^## /p' corpus/lessons/round-<N>.md | grep -c '^|'` must be >= 5 (header, separator, >=3 rows); every `source` cell must name an existing path or a runnable command.
1225:   - **Fails when.** The table is absent (rounds 68–76 carried numbers in prose only); a value has no source; a counter rises open→close and neither the report nor `## Limits` mentions it.
1226:   - **Shown able to fail.** Round 76: `open` proxy findings 3 and `open` README uncovered 1 are in receipts but no lesson table; the criterion makes the next round's absence a red row.
1227:   - **Limit.** It makes a trend visible; it does not plot, graph or threshold counters, and a counter absent from the table is out of scope. It does not replace Q70's transcript rule.
1228:   - **Supersedes.** None. Adds the trend half Q70 leaves to tallies.
1229: 
1230: - **Q22-C1 — Q22's axis-set command mis-parses a scorecard whose Axes rows carry escaped pipes (round 77, append-only).** Grounding: the round-77 report check — `awk -F'|'` splits the two live `coverage:*` rows on their escaped `\|` cells, so the scorecard side of the diff yields `grep -cE`, `js`, `js` beside the six real axes while the report side yields the six axes (`axis_diff=1` on a correct report). Q22's intent (the report's axis set equals the scorecard's) is unchanged; the extraction is corrected: `awk '/^## Axes/{f=1;next} /^## /{f=0} f' SCORECARD.md | grep -oE '^\| *(operability|coverage[^|]*) *\|' | sed -E 's/^\| *([^|]*) *\|.*/\1/; s/ +$//' | sort -u` versus the report's first table column, `sort -u`. A report is not non-conformant merely because the frozen `awk` command is noisy; it is non-conformant when the two sets differ under the corrected extraction. Supersedes Q22's command only, not its rule.
1231: 
1232: - **Q73 — a frozen counter's every arm must be derived from its own contract, checked before the freeze commit (round 79).** Grounding: round 79's C2 counter required "≥10 `POINTER_DEAD` lines, first `close/proxy-json.txt`" while the same contract said receipt-shaped tokens are never re-reported; the base control showed v3 already reports the six `close/*` pointers as `RECEIPT_MISSING`, so the arm could never hold with the no-duplicate rule (`.ufo/waves/round-79/plan.md` Amendment 2, `controls/c2-base.txt`). The L1's dry run caught it before any verdict; no criterion asked whether an arm's expected value is reachable under the contract's other clauses.
1233:   - **Who checks.** The lane L1 before the freeze/scaffolding commit; the freeze-review seat re-derives the arm set from the plan and the control receipts; the non-author closure re-runs one control.
1234:   - **Field.** For every frozen counter: the arm names in the counter and in the plan are the same set, and every arm's expected value is derivable from the contract sentence plus a control receipt (a measured base/stub reading, never a wish).
1235:   - **Command.** `grep -oE "^\s*\['[a-z0-9-]+'" .ufo/waves/round-<N>/probe/probe<N>-*.mjs | grep -oE "'[a-z0-9-]+'"` vs the arm names in the plan's `Counter arms` list; then for each arm whose expectation names a count or a first-element, point at the control receipt that measured it (`controls/`).
1236:   - **Fails when.** An arm can never hold under another clause of the same contract (the r79 C2 case); an arm's number is asserted without a control that measured it; the counter and the plan disagree on arm names.
1237:   - **Shown able to fail.** The r79 C2 arm 2 before Amendment 2: with the no-deduplicate rule applied the r78 report yields four `POINTER_DEAD` lines, never ten — the arm as written was unreachable.
1238:   - **Limit.** Proves reachability and agreement, not that the arms are decisive; a mutated control can still pass an arm set that is reachable but weak (the mutation batteries are the separate guard).
1239:   - **Supersedes.** None. Extends Q43/Q44's control discipline from targets to arm expectations.
1240: 
1241: - **Q74 — a lesson's Gate quotes record the quote's true word count, and the count is re-derivable from the capture (round 81).** Grounding: routed defects R80-5 and r79 D4 (two rounds recorded "21 words" for a 19-word quote; `corpus/lessons/round-80-verifier-spotcheck.md` §Discernment, `corpus/lessons/round-79.md` §Erratum). The Gate's per-row word count is the only machine-checkable part of the ≤25-word rule, and it was wrong twice.
1242:   - **Who checks.** The lane before committing a lesson with new rows; the non-author closure re-runs the command on the committed capture.
1243:   - **Command.** For every new Gate row, extract the quoted text (the exact bytes between the quote marks the row records), then `wc -w` over it, and compare with the number the row states: `python3 - <<'PY' … q=open('corpus/lessons/round-<N>.md').read(); …` — in practice the closure re-derives it with `grep -o '"[^"]*"' <capture> | grep -F '<first four words>'` plus `wc -w`. A row whose stated count differs from the measured count is a record defect, even when the quote is ≤25 words.
1244:   - **Fails when.** The stated count differs from `wc -w` of the quoted bytes; or the quote cannot be located verbatim in the committed capture (that is a fabrication check, Q3's sibling).
1245:   - **Shown able to fail.** Round 80's S119 row recorded 21 words for a 19-word quote; the same class recurred from round 79 (D4).
1246:   - **Limit.** Counts words, not whether the words ground the claim; a verbatim quote can still be irrelevant.
1247:   - **Supersedes.** None. Adds the arithmetic half of the ≤25-word rule to Q3's verbatim discipline.
1248: 
1249: - **Q75 — a stated tally is a pointer to a committed transcript, not prose (round 82).** Grounding:
1250:   `considerthese/2026-10-26.md` self-improvement idea 1 ("check that every number has a transcript"),
1251:   mined 2026-11-04 and opened at its own evidence — `corpus/lessons/round-81.md` §Routed-defect answers
1252:   (R80-8: the round-80 LOG stated 26 where the final suite was 34) and
1253:   `corpus/lessons/round-81-verifier-spotcheck.md` R81-4 (the ready-handoff knowledge entry quotes
1254:   `31/31 pass` while the shipped suite is 34/34). Idea 3 of the same file is **already implemented**
1255:   as Q68 and is not re-mined.
1256:   - **Who checks.** The lane before a round commit; the non-author closure re-runs the grep on the
1257:     committed tip.
1258:   - **Field.** Every `N/N pass`, `PASS (n cases)` or `MATCH pins=n` tally written into a report,
1259:     `LOG.md`, a knowledge entry or `SCORECARD.md` names a committed transcript that contains that exact
1260:     tally, or states the revision it was measured at when the tally is a run-time reading.
1261:   - **Command.** `grep -rnE '[0-9]+/[0-9]+ pass|PASS \([0-9]+ cases\)' <files>` then, per hit,
1262:     `grep -rlF '<tally>' .ufo/waves/round-<N>/ | head -1` — an empty result is an untranscripted tally.
1263:   - **Fails when.** A tally has no committed receipt containing it; a `verified-at` entry quotes a
1264:     tally from a revision other than the one it ships at, without naming the revision.
1265:   - **Shown able to fail.** Round 81's `corpus/knowledge/ready-handoff-admission.md` quoted 31/31 at a
1266:     tip whose suite is 34/34 (R81-4), and its LOG entry's 26 vs 34 (R80-8) — both found by the
1267:     outside check, not by the lane.
1268:   - **Limit.** Proves a transcript exists, not that it is the right transcript; a receipt from another
1269:     tool with the same tally still passes.
1270:   - **Supersedes.** None. Adds the pointer half Q74's word count leaves open.
