1272: ### Q76 — a round lesson's `## Gate` is checked against the landed registry in the same round (round 83; `considerthese/2026-10-26.md` idea 2)
1273: 
1274: - **Rule.** Every `S###` a round lesson's `## Gate` names must exist in `corpus/SOURCES.md` with the status
1275:   and anchor the Gate claims, checked before the lesson is committed. A Gate row is a claim about the
1276:   registry, not a note beside it.
1277: - **Command.** `grep -oE 'S[0-9]{3,}' corpus/lessons/round-<N>.md | sort -u | while read id; do grep -q "^| $id " corpus/SOURCES.md || echo "gate-absent:$id"; done`
1278:   — empty for a conformant lesson; pair it with the status/used-by census when the Gate states a status.
1279: - **Fails when.** A Gate row cites an id the registry lacks, or claims a status the registry does not carry
1280:   (round 65 D1's class: Gate rows mapping S204–S206 differently from the landed SOURCES).
1281: - **Shown able to fail.** Round 83's Gate names S240–S242 and the check prints nothing (all three present and
1282:   `mined`); the same check over a synthetic `S999` row prints `gate-absent:S999`
1283:   (`.ufo/waves/round-83/close/gate-registry-check.txt`).
1284: - **Limit.** Ids only — a Gate quote is not re-opened by this check; the non-author spot-check does that.
1285: - **Supersedes.** None. Adds the registry half of Q75's transcript rule.
1286: 
1287: ### Q77 — reconcile a counter headline with its executed arm rows (round 84)
1288: 
1289: - **Grounding.** `corpus/lessons/round-84.md` Mistakes, R83-D5: the frozen
1290:   round-83 counter declared 27 arms, executed 28, and printed HELD 27/27 with
1291:   one FAIL (`.ufo/waves/round-83/close/c1-probe.txt`).
1292: - **Rule.** New counters derive their denominator from their executable case
1293:   roster and refuse an executed-row count that differs. Before citing an
1294:   arm-form transcript's HELD headline, reconcile row count, unique names,
1295:   prefix, ok count, FAIL count, verdict and summary order.
1296: - **Command.** `node scripts/counter-receipt.mjs --receipt FILE`; the new
1297:   frozen `.ufo/waves/round-84/probe/probe84-c1.mjs` uses its table length and
1298:   checks ran equals that length, rather than an independent denominator.
1299: - **Shown able to fail.** On the unchanged r83 C1 receipt the named command
1300:   must exit 1 `ARMS_TOTAL`; on `close/c1-repair.txt` from r83 it must exit 0.
1301:   Observed commands and exits land in round-84 `close/history-red.txt` and
1302:   `close/history-repair.txt`, not a rewritten historical receipt.
1303: - **Limit.** Transcript consistency is not proof of semantic correctness,
1304:   complete expected-arm coverage, authenticity or process exit provenance.
1305:   Historical counters stay frozen; this rule adds no universal migration.
1306: - **Supersedes.** None; extends Q73's reachability check with runtime
1307:   reconciliation of the measured transcript.
1308: 
1309: - **Q78 — pre-data controls must be able to differ from the work.** Every claim
1310:   freezes, before its first data commit, four control classes scored by the same
1311:   frozen counter: (a) the do-nothing/base tree, (b) a constant printer, (c) a
1312:   label-keyed no-reader that never opens the input, and (d) a same-path content
1313:   variation (one path written N times with different content must yield N
1314:   distinct answers and distinct input-derived digests). Each control's expected
1315:   verdict is asserted exactly — exit code plus the derived line the counter
1316:   prints — and a control that reaches the target falsifies the counter, not the
1317:   claim. **Grounding:** round-84's `vacuous` row (`corpus/lessons/round-84.md`:
1318:   a six-line label-keyed no-reader printed the same 16 labels and reached
1319:   `held=16/16`, so the claim stopped) and round-85's remedy
1320:   (`corpus/knowledge/counter-receipt-discrimination.md`, S245; the three
1321:   controls score 1/20, 0/20 and 1/20 against the frozen 20-arm probe, and the
1322:   same-path control 0/3 for each). Scope: claims whose evidence is a counter's
1323:   own output; a claim evidenced by a committed artifact of another kind names
1324:   the equivalent control that skips its work.
1325: 
1326: ### Q79 — candidate measurements do not certify integrated bytes (round 86)
1327: 
1328: - **Grounding.** `corpus/lessons/round-86.md` Mistakes, attribution; R85-V3 in
1329:   `corpus/lessons/round-85-verifier-spotcheck.md`: the independent 41/41 receipt
1330:   named candidate `7659be6e…` while production held `f385bd7a…`.
1331: - **Rule.** Every new verification receipt names the full digest of the instrument
1332:   actually executed and the measured revision. A candidate run remains candidate-only
1333:   after integration; retain its receipt, then run the driver against the integrated
1334:   instrument before describing the result as integrated evidence. A digest alone
1335:   never certifies semantic correctness.
1336: - **Shown able to fail.** The two different historical digests above fail the identity
1337:   comparison even though the candidate transcript says 41/41. The new knowledge entry
1338:   relabels that result, and round-86 integrated receipts record their own tool digest.
1339: - **Limit.** This identifies a measurement's subject, not a trusted execution or
1340:   custody guarantee; it adds no claim about unexecuted checks.
1341: 
1342: ### Q80 — a receipt's digest must name the instrument its own command invoked (round 87)
1343: 
1344: - **Grounding.** `corpus/lessons/round-87.md` Mistakes, attribution; routed defect
1345:   R86-D1: `.ufo/waves/round-86/run-close.mjs:24` hashed `scripts/counter-receipt.mjs`
1346:   inside its per-case loop, so nine of ten round-86 close receipts named a subject they
1347:   never invoked (`.ufo/waves/round-87/open/census-toolbind.txt`: 239 receipts — 225 with
1348:   neither field, 4 with `cmd=` only, 10 with both and 9 of those mismatched).
1349: - **Rule.** A receipt that states a subject digest states it for the instrument named
1350:   by that receipt's own command line, at that receipt's own revision. A gate that binds
1351:   a receipt to its subject reads the receipt's `cmd=`, never a configured path, a
1352:   filename, or a directory name; a receipt with no command is `unchecked`, and a clean
1353:   verdict requires zero unchecked receipts as well as zero mismatches.
1354: - **Shown able to fail.** The frozen 12-arm scorer
1355:   (`.ufo/waves/round-87/probe/probe87-c1.mjs`) reads `DRIFT matched=1 mismatched=9` on
1356:   the round-86 bytes and flips on same-directory fixtures whose filename is unchanged;
1357:   the pre-data path-keyed control scores 3/12 and the constant controls 0/12 and 1/12
1358:   (`.ufo/waves/round-87/controls/*.txt`).
1359: - **Limit.** The binding is identity, not correctness: a matching digest says which
1360:   instrument produced the reading, never that the reading is right. An instrument
1361:   outside the lane cannot be revision-bound and is disclosed as `external=`.
1362: 
1363: ### Q81 — a binding predicate must make the judged revision and the worktree differ (round 88)
1364: 
1365: - **Grounding.** `corpus/lessons/round-87.md` survivor row. Round 87's frozen 12-arm scorer ran
1366:   on a clean lane, where the worktree and `--rev` hold the same bytes. K87Critic's
1367:   `cand-a-worktree.mjs` hashed `<lane>/<rel>` instead of the blob at the revision and still read
1368:   `C87_C1: HELD held=12/12` (`.ufo/waves/round-87/build/K87Critic/transcript-cand-a-worktree.txt:15`).
1369:   On a clone whose worktree was ahead of the judged revision it fell to 11/12 (`SCORES.md:26–27`).
1370:   The kill rule fired and C1 was UNMET.
1371: - **Rule.** A predicate that claims an instrument binds bytes *at a revision* scores that
1372:   instrument on a fixture where the judged revision, a second revision and the worktree hold three
1373:   different bytes for the same path. It also scores a path that exists only in the worktree. The
1374:   same scorer is run against the instrument's mechanical worktree twin (the revision read replaced
1375:   by a disk read and nothing else), and the twin must score below the target. A scorer whose
1376:   fixtures cannot make the two byte sources disagree has not tested revision binding, however
1377:   many arms it has.
1378: - **Check (mechanical).** Run from the lane root with `REV` = the measured revision and `S` a
1379:   fresh scratch dir. It passes iff it prints `Q81: PASS`:
1380: 
1381:   ```
1382:   S=$(mktemp -d -p /fast/scratch/hyaku) REV=$(git rev-parse HEAD); P=.ufo/waves/round-88/probe/probe88-c1.mjs
1383:   node .ufo/waves/round-88/controls/make-worktree-variant.mjs scripts/receipt-bind.mjs "$S/twin.mjs" &&
1384:   node "$P" --lane "$PWD" --work "$S/a" --rev "$REV" > "$S/int.txt"; i=$?;
1385:   node "$P" --lane "$PWD" --work "$S/b" --rev "$REV" --tool "$S/twin.mjs" > "$S/twin.txt"; t=$?;
1386:   n=$(grep -cE '^ARM (rev-receipt-wins|worktree-forgery|default-rev|untracked-instrument): FAIL' "$S/twin.txt");
1387:   [ $i -eq 0 ] && [ $t -eq 1 ] && [ "$n" -eq 4 ] && echo Q81: PASS || echo "Q81: FAIL int=$i twin=$t worktree_arms_failed=$n/4"
1388:   ```
1389: 
1390:   The integrated instrument holds, its twin is UNMET, and the twin is UNMET *because of* all four
1391:   worktree-sensitive arms rather than an unrelated one.
1392: - **Shown able to fail.** The committed pre-data controls `base-v1-worktree` (11/20) and
1393:   `r87-cand-a-worktree` (12/20) both fail all four arms
1394:   (`.ufo/waves/round-88/controls/base-v1-worktree.txt`, `r87-cand-a-worktree.txt`). Under the
1395:   round-87 scorer the same `cand-a-worktree` read 12/12, so a scorer without the three-body fixture
1396:   turns the check red. At `0ff3562f…` the integrated v2 read `C88_C1: HELD held=20/20` (exit 0). Its
1397:   twin read `C88_C1: UNMET held=11/20` (exit 1), and `worktree-forgery` read `CLEAN` there
1398:   (`.ufo/waves/round-88/build/K88ScribeEntry/q81-integrated.txt`, `q81-twin.txt`).
1399: - **Limit.** The check shows that the scorer *can* separate the two byte sources for this one
1400:   substitution, the one `make-worktree-variant.mjs` makes by rewriting `blobAt`. It does not show
1401:   that the instrument reads no other mutable state, and a candidate that renames `blobAt` makes
1402:   the generator refuse (exit 3) instead of producing a twin. An external instrument (absolute path
1403:   outside the lane) has no revision, so Q81 does not apply to it.
1404: - **Round-88 amendment (measured after the freeze, so it binds round 89, not round 88).** The
1405:   worktree twin is one forgery of many. Nine seat constructions reached 20/20 on the round-88 scorer
1406:   (`corpus/knowledge/receipt-subject-binding.md`, *Round 88 verdict*): the scorer must also make the
1407:   judged revision differ from HEAD and from the index, put an absolute in-lane token in front of a
1408:   dirty worktree, test each size/duplicate/escape boundary at its edge from both sides, and draw
1409:   fixture bytes and names at run time.
1410: 
1411: ### Q82 — a capability scorer may not hand the candidate its own fixture's identity (round 89)
1412: 
1413: - **Rule.** A scorer that reads only the candidate's stdout and exit code must not pass the candidate
1414:   an argument from which the expected verdict can be read off (a fixture directory named after the
1415:   arm, a file named after the behaviour, a constant body). If it does, a tool that computes nothing
1416:   reaches the terminal score, and the score measures the scorer, not the capability. Where an arm's
1417:   fixture has a *shape* (a bare-filename symlink target, a literal `/proc/self/root` prefix, one
1418:   leading U+FEFF), the arm must carry a **positive twin** that the same shape test gets wrong, so a
1419:   textual special case cannot pass.
1420: - **Grounding.** Round 89's frozen 30-arm scorer scored the lane's own v3 instrument 30/30 — and also
1421:   scored `cand-probe-keyed.mjs` 30/30: a tool that reads the `--dir` basename (`<arm>-<12 hex>`),
1422:   prints the verdict line that arm expects and computes nothing
1423:   (`.ufo/waves/round-89/build/K89Review/probe-cand-probe-keyed.txt`, re-run by the L1). A second
1424:   construction, `cand-skip-mode.mjs` (a textual `/proc/self/root` prefix strip and a blob-shape test
1425:   in place of the git mode test), also reached 30/30 (`probe-cand-skip-mode.txt`). Both are the
1426:   round-88 kill-rule class one level up: the scorer's fixtures are the defect, not the instrument.
1427: - **Who checks.** The L1 before freezing (a control that scores terminal by skipping everything), and
1428:   a reviewer seat that must attempt the probe-keyed construction explicitly.
1429: - **Field.** The scorer's fixture paths must not encode the arm; every shape-gated arm carries a twin
1430:   that breaks the shape; the scorer's own docstring names the fixture it actually builds.
1431: - **Command.** `node .ufo/waves/round-89/probe/probe89-c1.mjs --lane . --work "$HYAKU_SCRATCH/x" --rev <rev> --tool <probe-keyed construction>` — must print `C89_C1: UNMET`.
1432: - **Fails when.** Any construction that skips a claimed behaviour prints the terminal line, or a
1433:   shape-gated arm has no twin.
1434: - **Shown able to fail.** The probe-keyed construction prints `C89_C1: HELD held=30/30` exit 0
1435:   (round-89 finding, unedited probe; the defect is the arm fixtures, not the instrument). The positive
1436:   direction is round 89's own instrument: on the reviewer's D1 (a committed mode-120000 symlink whose
1437:   target has a space) and D3 (an in-lane instrument through a symlinked ancestor, dirty worktree) the
1438:   instrument answers `SYMLINK_INSTRUMENT` and `CLEAN` where both constructions answer `CLEAN` and
1439:   `DRIFT external=1` (`.ufo/waves/round-89/build/K89Review/demos.txt`).
1440: - **Limit.** The rule binds the scorer, not the instrument: it says nothing about whether the
1441:   instrument is right, and a scorer that satisfies it can still be blind to a behaviour nobody
1442:   thought to arm. Round 89's own probe remains the counter of record for its claim and is not edited
1443:   after data.
